","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.acme/commit/1bb2a62b846e49359986313a87be1399ea8e41a3","node_id":"C_kwDOI0nbCNoAKDFiYjJhNjJiODQ2ZTQ5MzU5OTg2MzEzYTg3YmUxMzk5ZWE4ZTQxYTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.acme/commit/b0050b798479640674f3d6be6726a93d2d1c0096","sha":"b0050b798479640674f3d6be6726a93d2d1c0096","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.acme/commits/b0050b798479640674f3d6be6726a93d2d1c0096"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.acme/commit/c16f3e2f55ee106263ee95e79c930a6216b79447","sha":"c16f3e2f55ee106263ee95e79c930a6216b79447","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.acme/commits/c16f3e2f55ee106263ee95e79c930a6216b79447"}],"sha":"1bb2a62b846e49359986313a87be1399ea8e41a3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.acme/commits/1bb2a62b846e49359986313a87be1399ea8e41a3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33319001?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chris299/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chris299/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chris299/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chris299/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/chris299","id":33319001,"login":"chris299","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzMzE5MDAx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chris299/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chris299/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chris299/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chris299/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chris299/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/chris299","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.acme/commits/f7b3d2993055fe477e72e2218d8120b7d4a3e178/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-21T10:34:51Z","email":"33319001+chris299@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Christoph Winkler"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-21T10:34:51Z","email":"33319001+chris299@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Christoph Winkler"},"message":"Restore POST-as-GET polling in ACME.js so orders can complete\n\nACME.js as published on npm cannot finish an order against today''s Let''s\nEncrypt. It re-sends two requests that Boulder rejects:\n\n  _postChallenge     a challenge that comes back \"pending\" from the trigger\n                     POST is triggered a second time; the repeat is answered\n                     with 409, which ACME.js misreads as a challenge status\n                     -> (E_STATE_UKN) challenge state ''409''\n\n  _pollOrderStatus   on \"processing\" the CSR is POSTed to the finalize URL\n                     again instead of polling the order URL as RFC 8555 7.4\n                     asks; the repeat is answered with orderNotReady, 403\n                     -> Didn''t finalize order: Unhandled status ''403''  (#49)\n\nBoth are races, which is why the same adapter version issues certificates for\nsome users and not others.\n\nUpstream fixed this in commit 0aa939a2, \"Bug fix: Polling status using\nPOST-as-GET wherever possible\", released as tag v3.1.1 in May 2021 and never\npublished to npm. src/lib/root-acme-post-as-get.ts carries those two\nfunctions verbatim from that tag and assigns them over the 3.1.0 ones before\nthe client is used. They are writable properties on the object require(''acme'')\nreturns, and the helpers they need are reachable from outside the package, so\nthis needs no network fetch, no postinstall, and no mutation of node_modules\n-- it also survives npm ci --ignore-scripts.\n\nVerified in an ioBroker dev environment (js-controller 7.2.2, admin 8.0.5)\nwith @root/acme 3.1.0 installed unpatched, ordering for a name never\nauthorized before so that the full challenge cycle ran: \"Collection dev1 order\nsuccess\", certificate returned by the staging CA.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f2cda1d1ae3340d98a252bebc94b1862078dedce","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.acme/git/trees/f2cda1d1ae3340d98a252bebc94b1862078dedce"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.acme/git/commits/f7b3d2993055fe477e72e2218d8120b7d4a3e178","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33319001?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chris299/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chris299/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chris299/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chris299/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/chris299","id":33319001,"login":"chris299","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzMzE5MDAx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chris299/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chris299/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chris299/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chris299/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chris299/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/chris299","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.acme/commit/f7b3d2993055fe477e72e2218d8120b7d4a3e178","node_id":"C_kwDOI0nbCNoAKGY3YjNkMjk5MzA1NWZlNDc3ZTcyZTIyMThkODEyMGI3ZDRhM2UxNzg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.acme/commit/b0050b798479640674f3d6be6726a93d2d1c0096","sha":"b0050b798479640674f3d6be6726a93d2d1c0096","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.acme/commits/b0050b798479640674f3d6be6726a93d2d1c0096"}],"sha":"f7b3d2993055fe477e72e2218d8120b7d4a3e178","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.acme/commits/f7b3d2993055fe477e72e2218d8120b7d4a3e178"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33319001?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chris299/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chris299/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chris299/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chris299/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/chris299","id":33319001,"login":"chris299","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzMzE5MDAx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chris299/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chris299/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chris299/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chris299/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chris299/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/chris299","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.acme/commits/c16f3e2f55ee106263ee95e79c930a6216b79447/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-21T10:00:49Z","email":"33319001+chris299@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Christoph Winkler"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-21T10:00:49Z","email":"33319001+chris299@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Christoph Winkler"},"message":"Do not assume a saved ACME account has a contact field\n\nEvery run after the first fails with\n\n  Failed in ACME init/generation: Cannot read properties of undefined\n  (reading ''0'')\n\nwhich means certificate renewal never happens: the first run registers an\naccount, and each later one dies before it looks at any collection.\n\nTwo separate problems in one line.\n\nThe crash. `accountObject.native?.full?.contact[0]` guards `full` but not\n`contact`. Optional chaining short-circuits the whole chain only when the\noperand of `?.` is nullish, so on the very first run -- no saved account, no\n`full` -- the `[0]` is never evaluated and nothing goes wrong. Once an account\nis saved, `full` exists, evaluation continues to `.contact` and then to `[0]`\non undefined.\n\nWhy contact is missing. Let''s Encrypt announced in January 2025 that it would\nstop sending expiration notifications, and it no longer stores contact\ninformation; its newAccount response no longer carries a `contact` field. A\nsaved account created since then legitimately has none, which is also why\nthis bites new installations rather than long-standing ones.\n\nSo guarding the index is not enough: comparing an absent contact against\n`mailto:...` is always unequal, and the adapter would then warn and register a\nfresh account on every run, walking into the registration rate limit. A\nmissing contact now means \"cannot verify\" and the saved account is kept.\n\nVerified in an ioBroker dev environment (js-controller 7.2.2, admin 8.0.5)\nagainst Let''s Encrypt staging, on one and the same saved account:\n\n  before  Loaded existing ACME account ... (no contact)\n          Failed in ACME init/generation: Cannot read properties of undefined\n  after   Loaded existing ACME account ... (same account, still no contact)\n          Collection winkler expiring soon - will renew\n          Collection winkler order success\n\nFixes #191\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ca0a9ab3faf018cb3de2802088266f7dbf0d770a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.acme/git/trees/ca0a9ab3faf018cb3de2802088266f7dbf0d770a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.acme/git/commits/c16f3e2f55ee106263ee95e79c930a6216b79447","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33319001?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chris299/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chris299/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chris299/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chris299/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/chris299","id":33319001,"login":"chris299","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzMzE5MDAx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chris299/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chris299/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chris299/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chris299/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chris299/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/chris299","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.acme/commit/c16f3e2f55ee106263ee95e79c930a6216b79447","node_id":"C_kwDOI0nbCNoAKGMxNmYzZTJmNTVlZTEwNjI2M2VlOTVlNzljOTMwYTYyMTZiNzk0NDc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.acme/commit/b0050b798479640674f3d6be6726a93d2d1c0096","sha":"b0050b798479640674f3d6be6726a93d2d1c0096","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.acme/commits/b0050b798479640674f3d6be6726a93d2d1c0096"}],"sha":"c16f3e2f55ee106263ee95e79c930a6216b79447","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.acme/commits/c16f3e2f55ee106263ee95e79c930a6216b79447"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33319001?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chris299/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chris299/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chris299/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chris299/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/chris299","id":33319001,"login":"chris299","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzMzE5MDAx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chris299/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chris299/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chris299/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chris299/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chris299/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/chris299","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.acme/commits/19d92d83445f4d78edc45bd0d63e8a02dcc3a0a8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-21T09:07:43Z","email":"33319001+chris299@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Christoph Winkler"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-21T09:07:43Z","email":"33319001+chris299@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Christoph Winkler"},"message":"Add support for eDNS.de DNS-01 challenge\n\neDNS.de offers a purpose-built DNS-01 challenge API. acme-dns-01-ednsde\nimplements the ACME.js challenge interface against it and has no runtime\ndependencies of its own.\n\nFive source changes plus the lock file and the rebuilt backend:\n\n- the dependency\n- the provider in the dns01Module select\n- the module name in the hidden expression of dns01Otoken, since a token is\n  the only credential eDNS needs\n- the module name in the dns01Module union in src/types.d.ts, without which\n  tsc rejects the switch case (TS2678)\n- the switch case itself\n\nThe switch case does two things that read as gratuitous without a reason.\n\nIt drops the generic propagationDelay. The plugin''s set() polls the zone''s\nauthoritative nameservers until every one of them serves the record and only\nthen returns, so it reports propagationDelay 0 and skipChallengeTest true\nfrom create(). Left in place, dns01PpropagationDelay from io-package.json is\nwritten over that 0 after creation and ACME.js waits a further two minutes\nfor a record it has already been told is in place. Netcup is special-cased\nfor the same reason.\n\nAnd it hands the plugin this.log.debug. eDNS answers a name it has already\npublished from a cache carrying the record''s own 300 s TTL, so a certificate\ncovering a domain and its wildcard waits that out once -- both challenges\nlive on the same _acme-challenge name. On the first live run the log went\nquiet for eleven minutes between \"will create\" and \"order success\", which is\nindistinguishable from a hang. The plugin is silent unless given somewhere to\nwrite.\n\nVerified in an ioBroker dev environment (js-controller 7.2.2, admin 8.0.5)\nagainst a live eDNS zone: a staging certificate covering winkler.tel and\n*.winkler.tel is issued and stored in system.certificates. The plugin also\npasses the acme-dns-01-test compliance harness.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"92d13ceb9f6f485f71f5c3acccb6f817ce3309af","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.acme/git/trees/92d13ceb9f6f485f71f5c3acccb6f817ce3309af"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.acme/git/commits/19d92d83445f4d78edc45bd0d63e8a02dcc3a0a8","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33319001?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chris299/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chris299/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chris299/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chris299/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/chris299","id":33319001,"login":"chris299","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzMzE5MDAx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chris299/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chris299/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chris299/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chris299/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chris299/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/chris299","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.acme/commit/19d92d83445f4d78edc45bd0d63e8a02dcc3a0a8","node_id":"C_kwDOI0nbCNoAKDE5ZDkyZDgzNDQ1ZjRkNzhlZGM0NWJkMGQ2M2U4YTAyZGNjM2EwYTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.acme/commit/b0050b798479640674f3d6be6726a93d2d1c0096","sha":"b0050b798479640674f3d6be6726a93d2d1c0096","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.acme/commits/b0050b798479640674f3d6be6726a93d2d1c0096"}],"sha":"19d92d83445f4d78edc45bd0d63e8a02dcc3a0a8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.acme/commits/19d92d83445f4d78edc4