://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/redhat-developer/rhdh/commit/41b94440cb868217e78b8d4cb3a0d6dfd4afee63","node_id":"C_kwDOI1ELK9oAKDQxYjk0NDQwY2I4NjgyMTdlNzhiOGQ0Y2IzYTBkNmRmZDRhZmVlNjM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/redhat-developer/rhdh/commit/93d36352b6acf6f0bf7e7e376349a1eb5d965344","sha":"93d36352b6acf6f0bf7e7e376349a1eb5d965344","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redhat-developer/rhdh/commits/93d36352b6acf6f0bf7e7e376349a1eb5d965344"}],"sha":"41b94440cb868217e78b8d4cb3a0d6dfd4afee63","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redhat-developer/rhdh/commits/41b94440cb868217e78b8d4cb3a0d6dfd4afee63"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1463004?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gustavolira/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gustavolira/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gustavolira/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gustavolira/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gustavolira","id":1463004,"login":"gustavolira","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0NjMwMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gustavolira/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gustavolira/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gustavolira/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gustavolira/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gustavolira/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gustavolira","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redhat-developer/rhdh/commits/93d36352b6acf6f0bf7e7e376349a1eb5d965344/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T15:44:37Z","email":"guga.java@gmail.com","name":"Gustavo Lira e Silva"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T15:44:37Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(e2e): deploy showcase-runtime with the 2.y chart values (#5537)\n\n* fix(e2e): deploy showcase-runtime with the 2.y chart values\n\nThe runtime deploy still generated values for the 1.x chart (upstream.*,\nglobal.clusterRouterBase, global.catalogIndex, global.lightspeed). The 2.y\nchart ignores those keys, so the release fell back to the chart default\nimage digest, which no longer exists on quay.io, and the route was created\non apps.example.com. The Helm runtime project has not run a single test\nsince the chart migration.\n\nGenerate the 2.y layout instead, and point every POSTGRES_* env var at\nthe schema-mode secret. The 2.y chart already sets POSTGRES_HOST, PORT and\nUSER as literal values, so the previous add-only patch kept user\n\"postgres\" with the restricted user''s password.\n\nFor the operator path, add a wait-for-db init container to the Backstage\nCR. Backstage can start before the headless PostgreSQL Service resolves;\nevery plugin then fails its DB setup with ENOTFOUND and the pod stays\nunready until it is deleted.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nSigned-off-by: Gustavo Lira e Silva <guga.java@gmail.com>\n\n* refactor(e2e): reuse the env-from-secret helper and cover runtime config\n\nReview follow-ups for the runtime deploy fix:\n\n- Schema mode now goes through KubeClient.addContainerEnvVarsFromSecret, the\n  helper the external DB flow already uses, instead of building its own\n  JSON patch. Its patch building moves to pure functions in\n  kube-client/helpers.ts (envVarsNotFromSecret, buildEnvFromSecretPatch), and\n  it now creates the env array when the container has none. Removing every\n  same-named entry also covers a variable defined twice.\n- generateHelmSetArgs builds the three image flag groups with one helper.\n- wait-for-db gets the same hardened securityContext as the chart''s init\n  container.\n- Comments: the file header no longer claims the arrays must be repeated in\n  full, and the system volume list names all volumes the chart owns.\n- Unit tests for the Helm args, the Helm values, the operator CR and the env\n  patch builders. Against the runtime-config.ts on main, 9 of the 11 new\n  config tests fail, including the ones that catch 1.x keys.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nSigned-off-by: Gustavo Lira e Silva <guga.java@gmail.com>\n\n* fix(e2e): allow backend egress for the runtime external DB tests\n\nThe 2.y chart ships default-deny NetworkPolicies that only allow the backend\nto reach the PostgreSQL in its own namespace. The runtime deploy did not add\nthe egress allowance CI applies to its other namespaces\n(netpol-ci-allow-backend-egress.yaml), so after the external DB tests point\nRHDH at Azure or RDS the backend can never connect and stays unready.\n\nOn the PR nightly, each Azure \"Configure and restart\" attempt ran into the\n10 minute test timeout, and every retry redeployed the namespace, until the\njob was killed after about two hours without reaching RDS, schema mode or\nthe sanity check.\n\nRender the same allowance through the chart''s extraDeploy.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nSigned-off-by: Gustavo Lira e Silva <guga.java@gmail.com>\n\n* fix(e2e): enable guest auth and keep schema mode off SSL in the runtime tests\n\nWith the runtime deploy working again, the PR nightly ran the external DB\ntests for the first time on the 2.y chart. Every \"Configure and restart\"\npassed, but two problems remained:\n\n- \"Verify successful DB connection\" failed for all Azure and RDS versions\n  with \"Failed to load user identity: 401 Unauthorized\". Auth providers are\n  no longer built into the backend, and the catalog index ships the guest\n  provider disabled, so the guest session had no user token. Enable the same\n  guest provider package values_showcase.yaml uses, in the Helm values and in\n  the operator dynamic plugins.\n- Schema mode timed out in beforeAll. Its internal DB connection had no ssl\n  setting, so pg fell back to PGSSLMODE=require, which the external DB tests\n  leave on the deployment, and the backend never connected to the non-TLS\n  internal PostgreSQL. Set ssl: false explicitly. The config moves to a pure\n  schemaModeDatabaseConfig() so it can be unit tested.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nSigned-off-by: Gustavo Lira e Silva <guga.java@gmail.com>\n\n* chore(e2e): use the guest provider build for Backstage 1.54.6\n\nMatch the latest overlay artifact (bs_1.54.6__0.2.22), which is built for\nthe Backstage version on main.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nSigned-off-by: Gustavo Lira e Silva <guga.java@gmail.com>\n\n* fix(e2e): enable the home page in the runtime Helm values\n\nWith guest sign-in working, the external DB \"Verify successful DB\nconnection\" tests and \"Verify RHDH is accessible with schema mode\" all\nlanded on \"ERROR 404: PAGE NOT FOUND\" at \"/\". The new frontend system ships\npage:home disabled, and the CI namespaces only get it from\ndynamic-plugins-config.yaml, which the runtime deploy does not use.\n\nEnable the same home extensions in the runtime app-config.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nSigned-off-by: Gustavo Lira e Silva <guga.java@gmail.com>\n\n* fix(e2e): pass digest-pinned images to the chart as digests\n\nparseCatalogIndexImage and buildImageRef keep a sha256 digest in `tag` with\nan \"@\" separator, but imageSetArgs always sent it to `.tag` and cleared\n`.digest`. The chart renders `.tag` as `repo:tag`, so a digest-pinned\nCATALOG_INDEX_IMAGE (or TAG_NAME) became `repo:sha256:...` and could not be\npulled. Send \"@\" references to `.digest` and leave `.tag` empty.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nSigned-off-by: Gustavo Lira e Silva <guga.java@gmail.com>\n\n* fix(e2e): treat duplicate env entries as not yet pointed at the secret\n\nenvVarsNotFromSecret used .some(), so a variable with both the secret\nreference and a leftover literal counted as done and schema mode skipped the\npatch that removes the literal. Require exactly one entry, the secret\nreference, matching the duplicate removal in buildEnvFromSecretPatch.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nSigned-off-by: Gustavo Lira e Silva <guga.java@gmail.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Gustavo Lira e Silva <guga.java@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"60458cdee7e405df5e055f7a483e17308528c9b1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redhat-developer/rhdh/git/trees/60458cdee7e405df5e055f7a483e17308528c9b1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redhat-developer/rhdh/git/commits/93d36352b6acf6f0bf7e7e376349a1eb5d965344","verification":{"payload":"tree 60458cdee7e405df5e055f7a483e17308528c9b1\nparent 4305f24827dd34dca73565787582092fa02bfc22\nauthor Gustavo Lira e Silva <guga.java@gmail.com> 1790783077 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790783077 +0000\n\nfix(e2e): deploy showcase-runtime with the 2.y chart values (#5537)\n\n* fix(e2e): deploy showcase-runtime with the 2.y chart values\n\nThe runtime deploy still generated values for the 1.x chart (upstream.*,\nglobal.clusterRouterBase, global.catalogIndex, global.lightspeed). The 2.y\nchart ignores those keys, so the release fell back to the chart default\nimage digest, which no longer exists on quay.io, and the route was created\non apps.example.com. The Helm runtime project has not run a single test\nsince the chart migration.\n\nGenerate the 2.y layout instead, and point every POSTGRES_* env var at\nthe schema-mode secret. The 2.y chart already sets POSTGRES_HOST, PORT and\nUSER as literal values, so the previous add-only patch kept user\n\"postgres\" with the restricted user''s password.\n\nFor the operator path, add a wait-for-db init container to the Backstage\nCR. Backstage can start before the headless PostgreSQL Service resolves;\nevery plugin then fails its DB setup with ENOTFOUND and the pod stays\nunready until it is deleted.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nSigned-off-by: Gustavo Lira e Silva <guga.java@gmail.com>\n\n* refactor(e2e): reuse the env-from-secret helper and cover runtime config\n\nReview follow-ups for the runtime deploy fix:\n\n- Schema mode now goes through KubeClient.addContainerEnvVarsFromSecret, the\n  helper the external DB flow already uses, instead of building its own\n  JSON patch. Its patch building moves to pure functions in\n  kube-client/helpers.ts (envVarsNotFromSecret, buildEnvFromSecretPatch), and\n  it now creates the env array when the container has none. Removing every\n  same-named entry also covers a variable defined twice.\n- generateHelmSetArgs builds the three image flag groups with one helper.\n- wait-for-db gets the same hardened securityContext as the chart''s init\n  container.\n- Comments: the file header no longer claims the arrays must be repeated in\n  full, and the system volume list names all volumes the chart owns.\n- Unit tests for the Helm args, the Helm values, the operator CR and the env\n  patch builders. Against the runtime-config.ts on main, 9 of the 11 new\n  config tests fail, including the ones that catch 1.x keys.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nSigned-off-by: Gustavo Lira e Silva <guga.java@gmail.com>\n\n* fix(e2e): allow backend egress for the runtime external DB tests\n\nThe 2.y chart ships default-deny NetworkPolicies that only allow the backend\nto reach the PostgreSQL in its own namespace. The runtime deploy did not add\nthe egress allowance CI applies to its other namespaces\n(netpol-ci-allow-backend-egress.yaml), so after the external DB tests point\nRHDH at Azure or RDS the backend can never connect and stays unready.\n\nOn the PR nightly, each Azure \"Configure and restart\" attempt ran into the\n10 minute test timeout, and every retry redeployed the namespace, until the\njob was killed after about two hours without reaching RDS, schema mode or\nthe sanity check.\n\nRender the same allowance through the chart''s extraDeploy.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nSigned-off-by: Gustavo Lira e Silva <guga.java@gmail.com>\n\n* fix(e2e): enable guest auth and keep schema mode off SSL in the runtime tests\n\nWith the runtime deploy working again, the PR nightly ran the external DB\ntests for the first time on the 2.y chart. Every \"Configure and restart\"\npassed, but two problems remained:\n\n- \"Verify successful DB connection\" failed for all Azure and RDS versions\n  with \"Failed to load user identity: 401 Unauthorized\". Auth providers are\n  no longer built into the backend, and the catalog index ships the guest\n  provider disabled, so the guest session had no user token. Enable the same\n  guest provider package values_showcase.yaml uses, in the Helm values and in\n  the operator dynamic plugins.\n- Schema mode timed out in beforeAll. Its internal DB connection had no ssl\n  setting, so pg fell back to PGSSLMODE=require, which the external DB tests\n  leave on the deployment, and the backend never connected to the non-TLS\n  internal PostgreSQL. Set ssl: false explicitly. The config moves to a pure\n  schemaModeDatabaseConfig() so it can be unit tested.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nSigned-off-by: Gustavo Lira e Silva <guga.java@gmail.com>\n\n* chore(e2e): use the guest provider build for Backstage 1.54.6\n\nMatch the latest overlay artifact (bs_1.54.6__0.2.22), which is built for\nthe Backstage version on main.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nSigned-off-by: Gustavo Lira e Silva <guga.java@gmail.com>\n\n* fix(e2e): enable the home page in the runtime Helm values\n\nWith guest sign-in working, the external DB \"Verify successful DB\nconnection\" tests and \"Verify RHDH is accessible with schema mode\" all\nlanded on \"ERROR 404: PAGE NOT FOUND\" at \"/\". The new frontend system ships\npage:home disabled, and the CI namespaces only get it from\ndynamic-plugins-config.yaml, which the runtime deploy does not use.\n\nEnable the same home extensions in the runtime app-config.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nSigned-off-by: Gustavo Lira e Silva <guga.java@gmail.com>\n\n* fix(e2e): pass digest-pinned images to the chart as digests\n\nparseCatalogIndexImage and buildImageRef keep a sha256 digest in `tag` with\nan \"@\" separator, but imageSetArgs always sent it to `.tag` and cleared\n`.digest`. The chart renders `.tag` as `repo:tag`, so a digest-pinned\nCATALOG_INDEX_IMAGE (or TAG_NAME) became `repo:sha256:...` and could not be\npulled. Send \"@\" references to `.digest` and leave `.tag` empty.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nSigned-off-by: Gustavo Lira e Silva <guga.java@gmail.com>\n\n* fix(e2e): treat duplicate env entries as not yet pointed at the secret\n\nenvVarsNotFromSecret used .some(), so a variable with both the secret\nreference and a leftover literal counted as done and schema mode skipped the\npatch that removes the literal. Require exactly one entry, the secret\nreference, matching the duplicate removal in buildEnvFromSecretPatch.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nSigned-off-by: Gustavo Lira e Silva <guga.java@gmail.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Gustavo Lira e Silva <guga.java@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvS5lCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAA4cQAF53LmMd3DV9a9S1FeqMRyx9\nGLcUkOwVHu/fn4oA/2gQU2kmpxuCTmhfKzT8ehaBVMu8oy22Uj/3Es4utEn6WZV8\nuhCGFvKT2ma+n2+iPb8HkO3ITRYV+FDStxj4u1muPee+C/gtYOQotodWxDMgbSff\nXA4Pm3ONduKFPY7l8