2504f7cbdfa04b19ab9c984f90fd2a75c1fa4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redhat-developer/rhdh/commits/c432504f7cbdfa04b19ab9c984f90fd2a75c1fa4"}],"sha":"656e363d135cfe2880e533ee0344fe2dbdc2fc93","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redhat-developer/rhdh/commits/656e363d135cfe2880e533ee0344fe2dbdc2fc93"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1463004?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gustavolira/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gustavolira/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gustavolira/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gustavolira/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gustavolira","id":1463004,"login":"gustavolira","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0NjMwMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gustavolira/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gustavolira/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gustavolira/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gustavolira/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gustavolira/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gustavolira","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redhat-developer/rhdh/commits/c432504f7cbdfa04b19ab9c984f90fd2a75c1fa4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T20:48:00Z","email":"guga.java@gmail.com","name":"Gustavo Lira e Silva"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T20:48:00Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(e2e): read the Created At cell from the live first row (#5552)\n\nThe \"Toggle ''CREATED AT''\" test captured the first row''s text right after\nclicking the sort header, then looked that row up again by its text. When the\ntable was still re-sorting, the captured row belonged to the previous order\nand moved to another page of the 104 components, so the lookup found nothing\n(\"element(s) not found\") on every retry.\n\nRead the Created At cell from the first-row locator instead, so each\nassertion retry sees the current first row. The unused text-based lookup\nhelpers are replaced by findColumnIndex.\n\nSigned-off-by: Gustavo Lira e Silva <guga.java@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"4702f2f2b8800e9ec7af56d22b56c49fe17a71a6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redhat-developer/rhdh/git/trees/4702f2f2b8800e9ec7af56d22b56c49fe17a71a6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redhat-developer/rhdh/git/commits/c432504f7cbdfa04b19ab9c984f90fd2a75c1fa4","verification":{"payload":"tree 4702f2f2b8800e9ec7af56d22b56c49fe17a71a6\nparent fa2481885dcd2b308c327c80b091c9b7759c0aca\nauthor Gustavo Lira e Silva <guga.java@gmail.com> 1790714880 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790714880 +0000\n\nfix(e2e): read the Created At cell from the live first row (#5552)\n\nThe \"Toggle ''CREATED AT''\" test captured the first row''s text right after\nclicking the sort header, then looked that row up again by its text. When the\ntable was still re-sorting, the captured row belonged to the previous order\nand moved to another page of the 104 components, so the lookup found nothing\n(\"element(s) not found\") on every retry.\n\nRead the Created At cell from the first-row locator instead, so each\nassertion retry sees the current first row. The unused text-based lookup\nhelpers are replaced by findColumnIndex.\n\nSigned-off-by: Gustavo Lira e Silva <guga.java@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvCQACRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA4BcQAJSysYpN9s4p+ModLpEZmoh5\nc9oi3Ip0Yl/HilbWstxkaWnjlOYSQX3TrOvhTvZIf8Bv/iZKBaxCdiHQ1yfRJPC0\n/FH9+NUC0VK+JarKdb8qZW3GpzbXyL3TDfh2S3BLfbhIlQG3RlnFjdsG8fb0yhHJ\nCWa56sG4WTrT2ikbaEGFhdSfhkblSlYOZbeV9+m6yfB0g0CuangJ+1BQPcGJCMOL\nIeXHIgGNBekn