GBT3Y5aZjQwYveVU/Keu1sIlY7W3EP\nnIjP3NrZGaENsJLAuhCM\n=ZTT3\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-29T06:34:07Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/redhat-developer/rhdh/commit/ce354caf7d1ca8a420b85ca15fcdfb27cb4f9985","node_id":"C_kwDOI1ELK9oAKGNlMzU0Y2FmN2QxY2E4YTQyMGI4NWNhMTVmY2RmYjI3Y2I0Zjk5ODU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/redhat-developer/rhdh/commit/0a2efdf3112b43b331b58df5c0fad7190a28703b","sha":"0a2efdf3112b43b331b58df5c0fad7190a28703b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redhat-developer/rhdh/commits/0a2efdf3112b43b331b58df5c0fad7190a28703b"}],"sha":"ce354caf7d1ca8a420b85ca15fcdfb27cb4f9985","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redhat-developer/rhdh/commits/ce354caf7d1ca8a420b85ca15fcdfb27cb4f9985"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1463004?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gustavolira/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gustavolira/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gustavolira/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gustavolira/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gustavolira","id":1463004,"login":"gustavolira","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0NjMwMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gustavolira/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gustavolira/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gustavolira/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gustavolira/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gustavolira/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gustavolira","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redhat-developer/rhdh/commits/0a2efdf3112b43b331b58df5c0fad7190a28703b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T13:24:32Z","email":"guga.java@gmail.com","name":"Gustavo Lira e Silva"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T13:24:32Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore(ci): run full tests and bump checks on Yarn patch PRs (#5521)\n\n* chore(ci): run full tests and bump checks on Yarn patch PRs\n\nCVE fixes shipped through the patch-backstage workflow land as Yarn\npatches. Turbo does not see a patch as a change to the packages that\nconsume it, so those PRs only built and tested `--affected` packages.\n\ndetect-backstage-bump now also flags a PR when it changes a file under\n.yarn/patches/, or when yarn.lock changes which patches are applied.\nSuch PRs build and test every package and run the Backstage bump checks\njob (config:check and the API surface diff).\n\nPatches of @backstage/* packages were already caught, because the patch\nhash is part of their yarn.lock resolution. This adds patches of other\npackages, such as the @janus-idp/cli patch from #4929, which the old\ndetection missed.\n\nRefs: RHIDP-13524\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(ci): state what the Yarn patch checks do not cover\n\nFor a Yarn patch, the full test run only reaches the patched code\nwhere existing unit tests already do, and the API surface diff only\ncovers @backstage/* packages. The previous wording called any new\nfailure \"a regression from the patch\", which overstated the gate.\nE2E remains the integration gate.\n\nOn release branches, patches under dynamic-plugins/.yarn/patches/ are\nnot detected, because the checks only cover the root Yarn project.\nSay so instead of implying coverage.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e2e05420ca425ad7426979c6026112801fd8a53b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redhat-developer/rhdh/git/trees/e2e05420ca425ad7426979c6026112801fd8a53b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redhat-developer/rhdh/git/commits/0a2efdf3112b43b331b58df5c0fad7190a28703b","verification":{"payload":"tree e2e05420ca425ad7426979c6026112801fd8a53b\nparent 2e92d1edbbc3322a210952a251c8212c2fff58ae\nauthor Gustavo Lira e Silva <guga.java@gmail.com> 1790601872 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790601872 +0000\n\nchore(ci): run full tests and bump checks on Yarn patch PRs (#5521)\n\n* chore(ci): run full tests and bump checks on Yarn patch PRs\n\nCVE fixes shipped through the patch-backstage workflow land as Yarn\npatches. Turbo does not see a patch as a change to the packages that\nconsume it, so those PRs only built and tested `--affected` packages.\n\ndetect-backstage-bump now also flags a PR when it changes a file under\n.yarn/patches/, or when yarn.lock changes which patches are applied.\nSuch PRs build and test every package and run the Backstage bump checks\njob (config:check and the API surface diff).\n\nPatches of @backstage/* packages were already caught, because the patch\nhash is part of their yarn.lock resolution. This adds patches of other\npackages, such as the @janus-idp/cli patch from #4929, which the old\ndetection missed.\n\nRefs: RHIDP-13524\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(ci): state what the Yarn patch checks do not cover\n\nFor a Yarn patch, the full test run only reaches the patched code\nwhere existing unit tests already do, and the API surface diff only\ncovers @backstage/* packages. The previous wording called any new\nfailure \"a regression from the patch\", which overstated the gate.\nE2E remains the integration gate.\n\nOn release branches, patches under dynamic-plugins/.yarn/patches/ are\nnot detected, because the checks only cover the root Yarn project.\nSay so instead of implying coverage.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqumqQCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAATWgQAC/hLRABiyK06eR/2wqknm3B\n/Ua5hGhUh7pa8FkWvppQQfAq2P9MsZfWEMYV9LXB5NfXV4fFzSSsqb7nj4C0IJ9G\nnr5gIqS+RA6cqBk1lPdQgOcDKpxsIqxLGjRAeoz8Gd8+uBjCTOm+hid00ZjAIL2b\nJyDeBhnD3AN5MtSLedGpRR+Y0bc1U2NV/QJyFT7y1K3ENTszFZdatyLEH4uamvpN\nYtMEDFTm3RkeGs+2mw78ODOXdWOr/DYhMQgiDhzqdJpWa2IYsL3T9CgtrlyY8Wuk\nkU7ZcdAe95MCddcwx+tB2EA9Zf+tLm0gvfVvfLuEW0dRjGyZVesY3I3+kA5UZBgp\nxswQXx2yMEAEn93qt58M3z+dVj0dlvNTdzxRijuYzMsXMtlgsTtcA5Ux3HTkwIQb\nI/Edfi7bWsT7rQM8Sd90fJdJxKudFKZ+UMco/yy5FRy9dRxjC8b4uhghxqNa35nt\nVo7xcp6nNuezSYjec+E5XA4ziMNNf7g1nvnEBclQsQ4uUwwfP3jSr7l5YcQvSKTO\nzMOmQwmMpEf3pYUFPUfzsfxie/KjvRPeKtY90yaJ/FYbKWTDFW5u8lY94GaVbRUf\n0soH55aNYBRy/HRgsRjYjEp6eFlLlN+0VAyAZ1ZioGnezxbGw85FUQtINwk1eedt\nHHO9VwxtQtYzIdI6VZtf\n=AMbQ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-28T13:24:32Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https:/