rhdh/commit/6797a90c51a3f224dcee77e77e64d5faf3b97471","sha":"6797a90c51a3f224dcee77e77e64d5faf3b97471","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redhat-developer/rhdh/commits/6797a90c51a3f224dcee77e77e64d5faf3b97471"}],"sha":"f6d6278fe63b0137503e8c4b4b22f54caa02ae4c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redhat-developer/rhdh/commits/f6d6278fe63b0137503e8c4b4b22f54caa02ae4c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61500440?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zdrapela/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zdrapela/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zdrapela/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zdrapela/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zdrapela","id":61500440,"login":"zdrapela","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxNTAwNDQw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zdrapela/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zdrapela/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zdrapela/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zdrapela/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zdrapela/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zdrapela","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redhat-developer/rhdh/commits/6797a90c51a3f224dcee77e77e64d5faf3b97471/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-24T14:44:47Z","email":"61500440+zdrapela@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Zbyněk Drápela"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-24T14:44:47Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"test(e2e): use PostgreSQL 18, test PostgreSQL in upgrade job and fix K8s jobs (#5478)\n\n* test(e2e): use PostgreSQL 18\n\nAssisted-by: OpenCode\n\n* test(e2e): migrate PostgreSQL during upgrades\n\nPreserve the previous chart database version and use a logical dump and restore when the target major changes. Keep RHDH offline until the restored data is verified.\n\nRefs RHIDP-13956, RHIDP-13961, RHIDP-14594\n\nAssisted-by: OpenCode\n\n* fix(e2e): resolve previous upgrade release\n\nSelect the highest existing release branch and its matching base image instead of assuming every intermediate stream exists. Wait for application pods to terminate before dumping PostgreSQL.\n\nRefs RHIDP-13956, RHIDP-13961, RHIDP-14594\n\nAssisted-by: OpenCode\n\n* fix(e2e): use previous chart for upgrade baseline\n\nRestore release-specific chart values and legacy image flags for 1.x upgrade baselines while keeping target deployments on the standalone chart.\n\nAssisted-by: OpenCode\n\n* test(e2e): remove allowInsecureImages\n\n* fix(e2e): capture upgrade failure context\n\nAssisted-by: OpenCode\n\n* fix(e2e): align K8s values with standalone chart\n\nAssisted-by: OpenCode\n\n* fix(e2e): apply runtime PostgreSQL image overrides\n\nAssisted-by: OpenCode\nSigned-off-by: Zbyněk Drápela <zbynek.drapela@gmail.com>\n\n* fix(e2e): retain upgrade failure diagnostics\n\nAssisted-by: OpenCode\nSigned-off-by: Zbyněk Drápela <zbynek.drapela@gmail.com>\n\n* refactor(e2e): pass baseline release explicitly\n\nAssisted-by: OpenCode\nSigned-off-by: Zbyněk Drápela <zbynek.drapela@gmail.com>\n\n* refactor(e2e): remove unused upgrade helpers\n\nAssisted-by: OpenCode\nSigned-off-by: Zbyněk Drápela <zbynek.drapela@gmail.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Zbyněk Drápela <zbynek.drapela@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"d50c7fa40e79fb084f7b416ca4b7ebcb52dea5eb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redhat-developer/rhdh/git/trees/d50c7fa40e79fb084f7b416ca4b7ebcb52dea5eb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redhat-developer/rhdh/git/commits/6797a90c51a3f224dcee77e77e64d5faf3b97471","verification":{"payload":"tree d50c7fa40e79fb084f7b416ca4b7ebcb52dea5eb\nparent 29f3871acd380b76fbd52faaf5fc9c142e24279c\nauthor Zbyněk Drápela <61500440+zdrapela@users.noreply.github.com> 1790261087 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790261087 +0000\n\ntest(e2e): use PostgreSQL 18, test PostgreSQL in upgrade job and fix K8s jobs (#5478)\n\n* test(e2e): use PostgreSQL 18\n\nAssisted-by: OpenCode\n\n* test(e2e): migrate PostgreSQL during upgrades\n\nPreserve the previous chart database version and use a logical dump and restore when the target major changes. Keep RHDH offline until the restored data is verified.\n\nRefs RHIDP-13956, RHIDP-13961, RHIDP-14594\n\nAssisted-by: OpenCode\n\n* fix(e2e): resolve previous upgrade release\n\nSelect the highest existing release branch and its matching base image instead of assuming every intermediate stream exists. Wait for application pods to terminate before dumping PostgreSQL.\n\nRefs RHIDP-13956, RHIDP-13961, RHIDP-14594\n\nAssisted-by: OpenCode\n\n* fix(e2e): use previous chart for upgrade baseline\n\nRestore release-specific chart values and legacy image flags for 1.x upgrade baselines while keeping target deployments on the standalone chart.\n\nAssisted-by: OpenCode\n\n* test(e2e): remove allowInsecureImages\n\n* fix(e2e): capture upgrade failure context\n\nAssisted-by: OpenCode\n\n* fix(e2e): align K8s values with standalone chart\n\nAssisted-by: OpenCode\n\n* fix(e2e): apply runtime PostgreSQL image overrides\n\nAssisted-by: OpenCode\nSigned-off-by: Zbyněk Drápela <zbynek.drapela@gmail.com>\n\n* fix(e2e): retain upgrade failure diagnostics\n\nAssisted-by: OpenCode\nSigned-off-by: Zbyněk Drápela <zbynek.drapela@gmail.com>\n\n* refactor(e2e): pass baseline release explicitly\n\nAssisted-by: OpenCode\nSigned-off-by: Zbyněk Drápela <zbynek.drapela@gmail.com>\n\n* refactor(e2e): remove unused upgrade helpers\n\nAssisted-by: OpenCode\nSigned-off-by: Zbyněk Drápela <zbynek.drapela@gmail.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Zbyněk Drápela <zbynek.drapela@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqtTdfCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAyRQQAEaot8hnK474RaVnWsDHgA+1\nv6hrVhG+kzfMel2u3G02wAllplEf9UuqkUSOW5nli9Krlf9xNlaV2NfHevNfbrQh\n