ar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/redhat-developer/rhdh/commit/3a33afc61bdf672fef35d7c96d1aa631e56e6cd0","node_id":"C_kwDOI1ELK9oAKDNhMzNhZmM2MWJkZjY3MmZlZjM1ZDdjOTZkMWFhNjMxZTU2ZTZjZDA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/redhat-developer/rhdh/commit/a5cf1001a736c450733ffefca9602781856df8d4","sha":"a5cf1001a736c450733ffefca9602781856df8d4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redhat-developer/rhdh/commits/a5cf1001a736c450733ffefca9602781856df8d4"}],"sha":"3a33afc61bdf672fef35d7c96d1aa631e56e6cd0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redhat-developer/rhdh/commits/3a33afc61bdf672fef35d7c96d1aa631e56e6cd0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1463004?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gustavolira/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gustavolira/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gustavolira/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gustavolira/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gustavolira","id":1463004,"login":"gustavolira","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0NjMwMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gustavolira/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gustavolira/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gustavolira/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gustavolira/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gustavolira/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gustavolira","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redhat-developer/rhdh/commits/a5cf1001a736c450733ffefca9602781856df8d4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-23T18:28:11Z","email":"guga.java@gmail.com","name":"Gustavo Lira e Silva"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-23T18:28:11Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(ci): repair K8s, disconnected and upgrade jobs after the chart 2.y migration (#5504)\n\n* fix(ci): repair K8s, disconnected and upgrade jobs after the chart 2.y migration\n\nThe chart 2.y migration (#5490, merged through #5503) was validated only\nby e2e-ocp-helm. Rendering the other jobs'' values against chart 2.0-90-CI\nshows six failures in jobs no PR check runs:\n\n- AKS (both namespaces) and GKE RBAC: ingress.host is not in the 2.y\n  schema, so helm fails schema validation. The host already comes from\n  --set host.\n- AKS/EKS/GKE RBAC: the diffs lost the database override, so the base\n  ssl config points at Crunchy cert files that are not mounted, and the\n  bundled Fedora postgres has no TLS. Null out ssl again.\n- AKS/EKS/GKE RBAC: the chart pins the RHEL postgres image by digest, so\n  overriding only registry/repository/tag rendered\n  fedora/postgresql-15@<RHEL digest>. Clear the digest.\n- ocp-disconnected-helm: add global.security.allowInsecureImages, which\n  Bitnami image verification requires for the RHEL postgres image.\n- ocp-disconnected-helm: read postgresql.image.digest, which 2.y uses\n  instead of encoding the digest in repository/tag, so the mirrored ref\n  matches the one the pod pulls instead of falling back to :latest.\n- e2e-ocp-helm-upgrade: the base install uses the previous release''s\n  1.x chart, which ignores the 2.y --set paths; restore the 1.x paths.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(ci): pick upgrade base flags by chart major and keep digest parsing on one path\n\n- initiate_upgrade_base_deployments hardcoded the 1.x value paths. That\n  is right while the previous release is 1.x, but once the base becomes\n  a 2.y chart (main moving to 2.1, or a preset CHART_VERSION_BASE) the\n  2.y schema silently ignores upstream.* and the base comes up with the\n  chart''s default image and host. Select the flag set by the base\n  chart''s major version.\n- ocp-disconnected-helm skipped common::normalize_chart_image_ref when\n  postgresql.image.digest was set, so a repository still carrying\n  @sha256 produced repo@sha256@sha256:<hash>. Always normalize, then let\n  the digest override separator and tag.\n- values_disconnected-smoke: move the allowInsecureImages block next to\n  the other chart feature flags instead of inside the dynamic plugins\n  comment.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"6822bcc61784a0e06b3c0c8646c116c068a58482","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redhat-developer/rhdh/git/trees/6822bcc61784a0e06b3c0c8646c116c068a58482"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redhat-developer/rhdh/git/commits/a5cf1001a736c450733ffefca9602781856df8d4","verification":{"payload":"tree 6822bcc61784a0e06b3c0c8646c116c068a58482\nparent b7d5217341eeaa71024a78e2bfeb65d3b07f45bd\nauthor Gustavo Lira e Silva <guga.java@gmail.com> 1790188091 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790188091 +0000\n\nfix(ci): repair K8s, disconnected and upgrade jobs after the chart 2.y migration (#5504)\n\n* fix(ci): repair K8s, disconnected and upgrade jobs after the chart 2.y migration\n\nThe chart 2.y migration (#5490, merged through #5503) was validated only\nby e2e-ocp-helm. Rendering the other jobs'' values against chart 2.0-90-CI\nshows six failures in jobs no PR check runs:\n\n- AKS (both namespaces) and GKE RBAC: ingress.host is not in the 2.y\n  schema, so helm fails schema validation. The host already comes from\n  --set host.\n- AKS/EKS/GKE RBAC: the diffs lost the database override, so the base\n  ssl config points at Crunchy cert files that are not mounted, and the\n  bundled Fedora postgres has no TLS. Null out ssl again.\n- AKS/EKS/GKE RBAC: the chart pins the RHEL postgres image by digest, so\n  overriding only registry/repository/tag rendered\n  fedora/postgresql-15@<RHEL digest>. Clear the digest.\n- ocp-disconnected-helm: add global.security.allowInsecureImages, which\n  Bitnami image verification requires for the RHEL postgres image.\n- ocp-disconnected-helm: read postgresql.image.digest, which 2.y uses\n  instead of encoding the digest in repository/tag, so the mirrored ref\n  matches the one the pod pulls instead of falling back to :latest.\n- e2e-ocp-helm-upgrade: the base install uses the previous release''s\n  1.x chart, which ignores the 2.y --set paths; restore the 1.x paths.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(ci): pick upgrade base flags by chart major and keep digest parsing on one path\n\n- initiate_upgrade_base_deployments hardcoded the 1.x value paths. That\n  is right while the previous release is 1.x, but once the base becomes\n  a 2.y chart (main moving to 2.1, or a preset CHART_VERSION_BASE) the\n  2.y schema silently ignores upstream.* and the base comes up with the\n  chart''s default image and host. Select the flag set by the base\n  chart''s major version.\n- ocp-disconnected-helm skipped common::normalize_chart_image_ref when\n  postgresql.image.digest was set, so a repository still carrying\n  @sha256 produced repo@sha256@sha256:<hash>. Always normalize, then let\n  the digest override separator and tag.\n- values_disconnected-smoke: move the allowInsecureImages block next to\n  the other chart feature flags instead of inside the dynamic plugins\n  comment.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqtBo7CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAjYMQAJNikaA1gEwr18kCU4RGJBR+\nioZTMlOFFEFnh2nxVaOn1Dh5W1FCphmlbg8bONabso5/g+PlFXpNn7cmcnrWiFct\nOtsJkf7Y0q+BfI/TF3GhLD7U9sfXEu6TIGQFCXG940ktKTYVNYG79t7hI7L6NMZ8\n7C6BuTfA27z75+ts4IyLyEgn/h9dPimEi8Cnbo2xm0iWLcR9X1xbyBJNkCq9HgY2\nfX2GS6zKRPfa9/dFb4zuo9ORZK8keXIcihFX8zJsShr5peMx4MUOIKpxEjSczq3y\nNCgbf+lgudtM6tZwbzm85flpYCXgn3kHdZbLhKSmpRNheb4CeoZ/xgU0ahEIAkpm\nPXa2tJ/HEXlOML/kWaX+jKa3URfJMAGKyxoprMw/djTwETUyuG/8wrcm8y6Kojqs\nHWNawrSzXDSI4BEJRwkRB95VbBUf6/N8tpLaX6Jp+akffOpRjc0LiJ5g9KBcrTeR\nb1lCwhz0jLkWakwJ8+TSeLkV766Rsm9+rXli+zYvbInkS7tF/VbOEatuEoldLLrD\nxUEyYh1opcJ+kcJ/vM99ZzzWn/oLXs3xxksPxHEK4A1wktu7uox6oelqooASDXZD\nCccsjNZ1IxqyK3eo8GPN+aaOi8AlDWshjIyX+BmdYbA3BpjCypHIvJ23wXogvWFa\nP85ZAFFge1oZLpt/LG4T\n=OC2G\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-23T18:28:11Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/redhat-developer/rhdh/commit/a5cf1001a736c450733ffefca9602781856df8d4","node_id":"C_kwDOI1ELK9oAKGE1Y2YxMDAxYTczNmM0NTA3MzNmZmVmY2E5NjAyNzgxODU2ZGY4ZDQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/redhat-developer/rhdh/commit/b7d5217341eeaa71024a78e2bfeb65d3b07f45bd","sha":"b7d5217341eeaa71024a78e2bfeb65d3b07f45bd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redhat-developer/rhdh/commits/b7d5217341eeaa71024a78e2bfeb65d3b07f45bd"}],"sha":"a5cf1001a736c450733ffefca9602781856df8d4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redhat-developer/rhdh/commits/a5cf1001a736c450733ffefca9602781856df8d4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/695720?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonkoops/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonkoops/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonkoops/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonkoops/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jonkoops","id":695720,"login":"jonkoops","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY5NTcyMA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonkoops/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonkoops/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonkoops/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonkoops/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonkoops/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonkoops","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redhat-developer/rhdh/commits/b7d5217341eeaa71024a78e2bfeb65d3b07f45bd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-23T16:20:23Z","email":"jonkoops@gmail.com","name":"Jon Koops"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-23T16:20:23Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(e2e): harden NFS settings pin and Docs coverage (#5503)\n\n* feat: migrate CI values files and scripts to new RHDH chart 2.y format\n\nThe downstream rhdh/chart has been restructured for 2.y — it now owns\nits templates directly instead of wrapping the bitnami backstage subchart.\nThis commit updates all CI values files and shell scripts to the new\nflattened path hierarchy:\n\n- global.dynamic → dynamicPlugins\n- upstream.backstage.* → root-level (image, appConfig, extraEnv, etc.)\n- upstream.postgresql → postgresql\n- upstream.volumePermissions → postgresql.volumePermissions\n- global.clusterRouterBase → openshift.clusterRouterBase\n- global.host → host\n- extraEnvVarsSecrets → extraEnvFrom (secretRef objects)\n- global.lightspeed → intelligentAssistant\n- global.catalogIndex.image → catalogIndex.image\n- route → openshift.route\n\nRemoves system volumes/mounts and auto-injected env vars (BACKEND_SECRET,\nPOSTGRESQL_ADMIN_PASSWORD) now managed by the chart. Aggressively\nsimplifies RBAC K8s diff files by dropping chart-defaulted config.\n\nAssisted-by: Claude\n(cherry picked from commit c7ce5cfdbe4ae367d31292f73429037a546c9217)\n\n* fix: ensure image digest is emptied when setting image tag via --set\n\nThe new RHDH chart has separate image.tag and image.digest fields.\nWhen setting a tag via --set, digest must be explicitly set to an\nempty string to prevent a pre-existing digest from taking precedence.\n\nAssisted-by: Claude\n(cherry picked from commit aad6b4dd9cd0f784c62091eee3c4a928baf93a1a)\n\n* fix(ci): align migrated CI value files with the chart 2.y schema\n\nThe chart 2.y values.schema.json rejects the leftover ingress.host key\n(ingress now takes a hosts array and stays disabled on OCP, where the\nRoute already derives its host from openshift.clusterRouterBase), so\nhelm install fails before deploying anything.\n\nTwo fixes carried over from the pre-migration value files, both verified\nagainst chart 2.0-90-CI with helm template:\n\n- global.security.allowInsecureImages: the chart replaces Bitnami''s\n  PostgreSQL image with registry.redhat.io/rhel9/postgresql-15 and the\n  Bitnami common chart refuses unrecognized images (bitnami/charts#30850).\n- intelligentAssistant.enabled: false: the flavour defaults to on and\n  injects a lightspeed-core sidecar these lanes do not test.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(ci): allow backend egress past the chart''s default-deny NetworkPolicies\n\nChart 2.y ships default-deny NetworkPolicies for the backend pod with\negress limited to DNS, HTTPS, Redis and PostgreSQL. The CI app-config\nproxies plain-HTTP routes (test-backstage-customization-provider for\nQuick Access, add-test-header), so those requests time out (HPM\nETIMEDOUT in the backend log) and every spec touching them fails.\n\nApply an additive CI-only NetworkPolicy that restores full egress for\nthe backend pod; the chart''s ingress restrictions stay untouched.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(e2e): align showcase tests with the current NFS header and sidebar\n\nThree showcase tests fail on every main PR run since 2026-09-22,\nindependent of the PR under test:\n\n- scaffolder-relation-processor searched for the \"test-relation-\"\n  prefix and opened the first hit. GitHub discovery also ingests the\n  leftover test-relation-* repos in the janus-qe org, so the test opened\n  a stale component without the scaffoldedFrom relation. Open the\n  component scaffolded by this run instead.\n- The global header profile button''s accessible name is now \"Settings\";\n  the user name is only its text. Match the button by text.\n- A collapsed sidebar keeps each link''s aria-label, so the APIs link is\n  still exposed by role. Assert the visible label is hidden instead.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(e2e): accept the TechDocs empty state in the Docs sidebar check\n\nThe cluster-free harness has no techdocs-annotated entities, so the\nTechDocs index renders only its \"No documentation available\" empty\nstate, without the \"Docs\" page header. Assert the /docs URL and accept\neither the header or the empty state.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(ci): configure scaffolder relation pair on the catalog-graph card\n\nWith the correct component now opened, the Overview Relations card still\ndrew only the root node: the runtime catalog-graph API (provided by the\napp-defaults plugin override) does not include the scaffolderOf /\nscaffoldedFrom pair from the scaffolder-relation-processor, so the edge\nis filtered out. Configure relations and relationPairs on\nentity-card:catalog-graph/relations directly, which takes precedence\nover the API defaults.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(e2e): harden NFS settings pin and Docs coverage\n\nOpen settings via the shared helper, assert pin toggle with sidebar\ncollapsed/expanded classes, and drop Docs from the cluster-free suite\nwhere the index is always empty.\n\nSigned-off-by: Jon Koops <jonkoops@gmail.com>\n\n* fix(e2e): add Unicode flag to oxlint regex literals\n\nSigned-off-by: Jon Koops <jonkoops@gmail.com>\n\n* fix(e2e): assert sidebar pin via text visibility\n\nProduction JSS minifies BackstageSidebarItem class names, so the\ncollapsed/expanded class checks only worked on the local webpack harness.\n\nSigned-off-by: Jon Koops <jonkoops@gmail.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Jon Koops <jonkoops@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Armel Soro <asoro@redhat.com>\nCo-authored-by: Gustavo Lira e Silva <guga.java@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"1bb87cea7faeef8348e6da3dd9ebcdd2f0b3b41e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redhat-developer/rhdh/git/trees/1bb87cea7faeef8348e6da3dd9ebcdd2f0b3b41e"},"url"