gress.host key\n(ingress now takes a hosts array and stays disabled on OCP, where the\nRoute already derives its host from openshift.clusterRouterBase), so\nhelm install fails before deploying anything.\n\nTwo fixes carried over from the pre-migration value files, both verified\nagainst chart 2.0-90-CI with helm template:\n\n- global.security.allowInsecureImages: the chart replaces Bitnami''s\n  PostgreSQL image with registry.redhat.io/rhel9/postgresql-15 and the\n  Bitnami common chart refuses unrecognized images (bitnami/charts#30850).\n- intelligentAssistant.enabled: false: the flavour defaults to on and\n  injects a lightspeed-core sidecar these lanes do not test.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(ci): allow backend egress past the chart''s default-deny NetworkPolicies\n\nChart 2.y ships default-deny NetworkPolicies for the backend pod with\negress limited to DNS, HTTPS, Redis and PostgreSQL. The CI app-config\nproxies plain-HTTP routes (test-backstage-customization-provider for\nQuick Access, add-test-header), so those requests time out (HPM\nETIMEDOUT in the backend log) and every spec touching them fails.\n\nApply an additive CI-only NetworkPolicy that restores full egress for\nthe backend pod; the chart''s ingress restrictions stay untouched.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(e2e): align showcase tests with the current NFS header and sidebar\n\nThree showcase tests fail on every main PR run since 2026-09-22,\nindependent of the PR under test:\n\n- scaffolder-relation-processor searched for the \"test-relation-\"\n  prefix and opened the first hit. GitHub discovery also ingests the\n  leftover test-relation-* repos in the janus-qe org, so the test opened\n  a stale component without the scaffoldedFrom relation. Open the\n  component scaffolded by this run instead.\n- The global header profile button''s accessible name is now \"Settings\";\n  the user name is only its text. Match the button by text.\n- A collapsed sidebar keeps each link''s aria-label, so the APIs link is\n  still exposed by role. Assert the visible label is hidden instead.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(e2e): accept the TechDocs empty state in the Docs sidebar check\n\nThe cluster-free harness has no techdocs-annotated entities, so the\nTechDocs index renders only its \"No documentation available\" empty\nstate, without the \"Docs\" page header. Assert the /docs URL and accept\neither the header or the empty state.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(ci): configure scaffolder relation pair on the catalog-graph card\n\nWith the correct component now opened, the Overview Relations card still\ndrew only the root node: the runtime catalog-graph API (provided by the\napp-defaults plugin override) does not include the scaffolderOf /\nscaffoldedFrom pair from the scaffolder-relation-processor, so the edge\nis filtered out. Configure relations and relationPairs on\nentity-card:catalog-graph/relations directly, which takes precedence\nover the API defaults.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(e2e): harden NFS settings pin and Docs coverage\n\nOpen settings via the shared helper, assert pin toggle with sidebar\ncollapsed/expanded classes, and drop Docs from the cluster-free suite\nwhere the index is always empty.\n\nSigned-off-by: Jon Koops <jonkoops@gmail.com>\n\n* fix(e2e): add Unicode flag to oxlint regex literals\n\nSigned-off-by: Jon Koops <jonkoops@gmail.com>\n\n* fix(e2e): assert sidebar pin via text visibility\n\nProduction JSS minifies BackstageSidebarItem class names, so the\ncollapsed/expanded class checks only worked on the local webpack harness.\n\nSigned-off-by: Jon Koops <jonkoops@gmail.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Jon Koops <jonkoops@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Armel Soro <asoro@redhat.com>\nCo-authored-by: Gustavo Lira e Silva <guga.java@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fab