avolira/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gustavolira/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gustavolira","id":1463004,"login":"gustavolira","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0NjMwMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gustavolira/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gustavolira/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gustavolira/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gustavolira/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gustavolira/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gustavolira","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redhat-developer/rhdh/commits/315dbb0f6d4c2716899c5556038a557a333e170d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-22T11:45:53Z","email":"guga.java@gmail.com","name":"Gustavo Lira e Silva"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-22T11:45:53Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(ci): merge the AWS RDS global CA bundle into the RDS trust store (#5447)\n\n* fix(ci): merge the AWS RDS global CA bundle into the RDS trust store\n\nThe RDS TLS e2e tests fail with SELF_SIGNED_CERT_IN_CHAIN on all four RDS\ninstances: the Vault copy of rds-db-certificates.pem no longer validates\nthe servers'' certificate chains (AWS rotates RDS CAs, and GSM cannot hold\nthe full global bundle — RHDHBUGS-3744 — so the stored copy is a trimmed\nsnapshot that goes stale).\n\nDownload the official AWS RDS global trust bundle at env-setup time and\nmerge the Vault copy into it, pointing RDS_DB_CERTIFICATES_PATH at the\nmerged file. Both consumers pick it up: the harness pg client\n(clearDatabase) and the postgres-crt secret mounted into RHDH\n(configurePostgresCertificate). If the download fails, fall back to the\nVault copy alone (current behavior).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(ci): keep the Vault CA path if writing the merged bundle fails\n\nReview follow-up: under errexit a double failure of the cat/cp fallback\nchain would abort the whole job before the cleanup trap is installed;\nguard it and keep pointing at the Vault copy in that case.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(ci): enforce HTTPS on the RDS bundle download redirects\n\nSonarCloud: curl -L could follow a redirect to a non-HTTPS target;\nrestrict both the initial request and any redirect to HTTPS.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"6df17bf24a4efa5bcfc35519f8c5911ec71032c7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redhat-developer/rhdh/git/trees/6df17bf24a4efa5bcfc35519f8c5911ec71032c7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redhat-developer/rhdh/git/commits/315dbb0f6d4c2716899c5556038a557a333e170d","verification":{"payload":"tree 6df17bf24a4efa5bcfc35519f8c5911ec71032c7\nparent f41b86a83b9706fb434f9de196cba8e1bcf6b287\nauthor Gustavo Lira e Silva <guga.java@gmail.com> 1790077553 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790077553 +0000\n\nfix(ci): merge the AWS RDS global CA bundle into the RDS trust store (#5447)\n\n* fix(ci): merge the AWS RDS global CA bundle into the RDS trust store\n\nThe RDS TLS e2e tests fail with SELF_SIGNED_CERT_IN_CHAIN on all four RDS\ninstances: the Vault copy of rds-db-certificates.pem no longer validates\nthe servers'' certificate chains (AWS rotates RDS CAs, and GSM cannot hold\nthe full global bundle — RHDHBUGS-3744 — so the stored copy is a trimmed\nsnapshot that goes stale).\n\nDownload the official AWS RDS global trust bundle at env-setup time and\nmerge the Vault copy into it, pointing RDS_DB_CERTIFICATES_PATH at the\nmerged file. Both consumers pick it up: the harness pg client\n(clearDatabase) and the postgres-crt secret mounted into RHDH\n(configurePostgresCertificate). If the download fails, fall back to the\nVault copy alone (current behavior).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(ci): keep the Vault CA path if writing the merged bundle fails\n\nReview follow-up: under errexit a double failure of the cat/cp fallback\nchain would abort the whole job before the cleanup trap is installed;\nguard it and keep pointing at the Vault copy in that case.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(ci): enforce HTTPS on the RDS bundle download redirects\n\nSonarCloud: curl -L could follow a redirect to a non-HTTPS target;\nrestrict both the initial request and any redirect to HTTPS.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqsmpxCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAABEAQAD7H5EzwPAgoJvHEybOwmv+o\nc/XBJYYugP1cx03AMU78Gv2DbiWe8TxW6Tgf3DSMD5VpU4R39htTGpHy5xSQbyhg\nuD6gfbc5f6lnJM/HwrbSk8Ex/BsHSnGCAcUCy4zxxt6fLYVAfL8fmlrR7BMBolQ4\nl89BgkptACr5gJ7GIQSLeC4Huq/1TiRi3rNi8MiCu8YsPwupIaQ2BEQB5IyC9G0h\nGYKFcd+Kwbd0ogbFJ4Aw2hnZZZagkB4BAKwUUOrCJapGq/wroxQLEjLHJtXxjVFH\nYtzppnmPiE6UTUSjf0KMVbGunPBM8nBocY7e3wPWtc7pn7tHyRiVHLkddg9/GXEj\n97Yb7n8H8MYl0UKnTMsi9+ooC64uSbnMClSzLCmIF+WKEM93o+ChMr8QU91X/TB4\nnd/X+wDIwq4MAWhmdze82E+44VmoikCP9QhSaDgOyrv6Fonnd+3Bt9BvNoztX84k\nWydqEI4I3kKneqfgE8DPhNhDlbnIldWzx4Wzia53+SwKXELID0Yq+8lOporRbwKa\nJxM1Q8w6iNnhE8sxE5f8l1/lAVvQ6f0XKTYMyd103JpLvwf+94npiyW/fdwjY7wm\nKQqVfZoYVMyT5aD2TEJCXs/UCviurnmxjIM8L9gjqwdCAGNmlZrEPoO6MTa0zkCb\nk5vdD3c9jqCdOJIwTWY4\n=MCUb\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-22T11:45:53Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/redhat-developer/rhdh/commit/315dbb0f6d4c2716899c5556038a557a333e170d","node_id":"C_kwDOI1ELK9oAKDMxNWRiYjBmNmQ0YzI3MTY4OTljNTU1NjAzOGE1NTdhMzMzZTE3MGQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/redhat-developer/rhdh/commit/f41b86a83b9706fb434f9de196cba8e1bcf6b287","sha":"f41b86a83b9706fb434f9de196cba8e1bcf6b287","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redhat-developer/rhdh/commits/f41b86a83b9706fb434f9de196cba8e1bcf6b287"}],"sha":"315dbb0f6d4c2716899c5556038a557a333e170d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redhat-developer/rhdh/commits/315dbb0f6d4c2716899c5556038a557a333e170d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1463004?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gustavolira/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gustavolira/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gustavolira/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gustavolira/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gustavolira","id":1463004,"login":"gustavolira","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0NjMwMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gustavolira/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gustavolira/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gustavolira/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gustavolira/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gustavolira/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gustavolira","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redhat-developer/rhdh/commits/f41b86a83b9706fb434f9de196cba8e1bcf6b287/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-22T11:21:35Z","email":"guga.java@gmail.com","name":"Gustavo Lira e Silva"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-22T11:21:35Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(ci): override stale RELATED_IMAGE_backstage digest in the operator CSV (#5435)\n\n* fix(ci): override stale RELATED_IMAGE_backstage digest in the operator CSV\n\nThe RHDH operator bundle CSV pins RELATED_IMAGE_backstage to the hub image\ndigest captured at bundle build time. The current next bundle (built\n2026-08-31) still pins the 2026-08-04 hub digest, whose bundled\ninstall-dynamic-plugins 0.4.0 resolves ref:// references only after the\npre-merge disabled pass and crash-loops with:\n\n  InstallException: Cannot resolve ref:// reference: no plugin named\n  ''backstage-community-plugin-catalog-backend-module-keycloak'' found in\n  included plugins\n\nThe Backstage CR deployment.patch already overrides both containers to\n$IMAGE_REGISTRY/$IMAGE_REPO:$TAG_NAME, but the installed operator applies\nthe RELATED_IMAGE_backstage env to the install-dynamic-plugins init\ncontainer after patching, so the stale digest wins there. This has kept\nshowcase-operator deployments red on OSD-GCP, GKE and AKS since early\nAugust (zero tests executed).\n\nPatch the CSV env right after operator installation so OLM propagates the\nimage under test to the operator deployment, and wait for the rollout.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(ci): guard command substitutions in the CSV override under errexit\n\nopenshift-ci-tests.sh runs with set -o errexit, so an empty grep result or\na missing deployment in the assignment pipelines would abort the whole job\ninstead of reaching the intended skip guards.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(ci): harden the CSV backstage image override against races and OLM v1\n\nReview follow-ups:\n- install-rhdh-catalog-source.sh returns right after creating the\n  Subscription, so poll for the CSV to appear before patching instead of\n  silently skipping on the common race.\n- Skip immediately (with a log) when RHDH was installed via an OLM v1\n  ClusterExtension, which has no CSV to patch.\n- Fail instead of skipping when the CSV exists but cannot be read, so an\n  API error is not masked as a legitimate skip.\n- Guard the rollout wait with an explicit log::error, and jq exit status\n  can no longer abort the script via errexit.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(ci): force the OLM v0 install path so the CSV override can apply\n\nThe osd-gcp run on this PR showed install-rhdh-catalog-source.sh\nauto-detecting OLM v1 on OCP/OSD >= 4.18 and installing via\nClusterExtension — no CSV exists there, override_operator_backstage_image\ntakes its skip guard, and the stale RELATED_IMAGE_backstage digest stays\nin effect (init container still crash-loops on ref:// resolution).\n\nPass --olm-version v0 so the standard operator jobs keep the CSV-based\ninstall that the override patches. OLM v1 coverage keeps its dedicated\nflows (disconnected jobs, RHIDP-14647).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(ci): wait for the image-registry default route before the operator install\n\nSame RHDHBUGS-3758 hardening as on release-1.9: the install script\npatches the registry and reads default-route before OpenShift creates\nit, intermittently failing the install. Expose and wait up front;\nwarn-only on timeout.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(ci): probe the registry through the default route before installing\n\nThe Route object existing is not enough: right after creation the\nrouter/registry data path can still refuse blob uploads (EOF on the\noperator bundle push, RHDHBUGS-3759). Poll the registry API through the\nroute until it answers 200/401 before handing off to the install script.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a26e5637ee66b2fcb8e5c76c520162a806ec4c28","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redhat-developer/rhdh/git/trees/a26e5637ee66b2fcb8e5c76c520162a806ec4c28"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redhat-developer/rhdh/git/commits/f41b86a83b9706fb434f9de196cba8e1bcf6b287","verification":{"payload":"tree a26e5637ee66b2fcb8e5c76c520162a806ec4c28\nparent f940cef543cec79df60f00756a59532fd0a4cc9f\nauthor Gustavo Lira e Silva <guga.java@gmail.com> 1790076095 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790076095 +0000\n\nfix(ci): override stale RELATED_IMAGE_backstage digest in the operator CSV (#5435)\n\n* fix(ci): override stale RELATED_IMAGE_backstage digest in the operator CSV\n\nThe RHDH operator bundle CSV pins RELATED_IMAGE_backstage to the hub image\ndigest captured at bundle build time. The current next bundle (built\n2026-08-31) still pins the 2026-08-04 hub digest, whose bundled\ninstall-dynamic-plugins 0.4.0 resolves ref:// references only after the\npre-merge disabled pass and crash-loops with:\n\n  InstallException: Cannot resolve ref:// reference: no plugin named\n  ''backstage-community-plugin-catalog-backend-module-keycloak'' found in\n  included plugins\n\nThe Backstage CR deployment.patch already overrides both containers to\n$IMAGE_REGISTRY/$IMAGE_REPO:$TAG_NAME, but the installed operator applies\nthe RELATED_IMAGE_backstage env to the install-dynamic-plugins init\ncontainer after patching, so the stale digest wins there. This has kept\nshowcase-operator deployments red on OSD-GCP, GKE and AKS since early\nAugust (zero tests executed).\n\nPatch the CSV env right after operator installation so OLM propagates the\nimage under test to the operator deployment, and wait for the rollout.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(ci): guard command substitutions in the CSV override under errexit\n\nopenshift-ci-tests.sh runs with set -o errexit, so an empty grep result or\na missing deployment in the assignment pipelines would abort the whole job\ninstead of reaching the intended skip guards.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(ci): harden the CSV backstage image override against races and OLM v1\n\nReview follow-ups:\n- install-rhdh-catalog-source.sh returns right after creating the\n  Subscription, so poll for the CSV to appear before patching instead of\n  silently skipping on the common race.\n- Skip immediately (with a log) when RHDH was installed via an OLM v1\n  ClusterExtension, which has no CSV to patch.\n- Fail instead of skipping when the CSV exists but cannot be read, so an\n  API error is not masked as a legitimate skip.\n- Guard the rollout wait with an explicit log::error, and jq exit status\n  can no longer abort the script via errexit.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(ci): force the OLM v0 install path so the CSV override can apply\n\nThe osd-gcp run on this PR showed install-rhdh-catalog-source.sh\nauto-detecting OLM v1 on OCP/OSD >= 4.18 and installing via\nClusterExtension — no CSV exists there, override_operator_backstage_image\ntakes its skip guard, and the stale RELATED_IMAGE_backstage digest stays\nin effect (init container still crash-loops on ref:// resolution).\n\nPass --olm-version v0 so the standard operator jobs keep the CSV-based\ninstall that the override patches. OLM v1 coverage keeps its dedicated\nflows (disconnected jobs, RHIDP-14647).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(ci): wait for the image-registry default route before the operator install\n\nSame RHDHBUGS-3758 hardening as on release-1.9: the install script\npatches the registry and reads default-route before OpenShift creates\nit, intermittently failing the install. Expose and wait up front;\nwarn-only on timeout.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(ci): probe the registry through the default route before installing\n\nThe Route object existing is not enough: right after creation the\nrouter/registry data path can still refuse blob uploads (EOF on the\noperator bundle push, RHDHBUGS-3759). Poll the registry API through the\nroute until it answers 200/401 before handing off to the install script.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqsmS/CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAPVoQACrqH2D0uGIUJu3Pa7TfvEHf\nf3ZE6rFN+cxJd/1iNdxkud/hLhbHD2AArR7Fq1sNQxApHPx5Hj4sayUrm61ZRO7Q\nT6o7mFHelFUS2gdOOKkT/tuIFPX+uYGY7y1thcOJFYA0t4AZ3igh/1r9XYoYL5ym\nenGpojcOND/y7VZqdAmQxsk4VxNSs9eR/e99mnJuhSXo/A6Qt5SJykXlT+4pLfuy\n4wo54CNnB4cz9hbkq4iEHBSkp58WbRYuDAxGnwmPRWJGcyQfByj+V6/0eFc74Bmp\nTq5u8b6EEI0u7W/zpq4Z4hfSUyaOvb30mdpZF8ZFLsrOJxPP4iUhmuMTUMpoY/4e\nM4zs7faSg5rZa3dTxMgMcCnwYJbnNcwUA/mdMYjAUPZxKwvVdSVJGbhhgKpRyde0\nifuC0rDsKgByawicZtKo2VZsa+NKxbFzorLovD51y0xXdNDlA0KXK5a7eU8iYeXR\noE2xwiP7BXiOJ/w4+sYgvZPWp3h9rFoTPzdlryTM92M2DWO17aarQ7OcK0UtU86a\nAPt3pu0/AcdkmhkDTk7kWsEoQ3oL5zVUTH2y9BeEZ8lWsqxxpio+cDeqyNf2nwXS\nuPaagItcpI6d/rx3ZOWhKnRTFIEHeXwuNvYCz/WA26JIF1LlGlEQXeof44aFv55N\nLEqZfnLsZ9OLLIB4rVbn\n=by96\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-22T11:21:36Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-f