b53dbde8514011e0329aa7143d540","node_id":"C_kwDOI1ELK9oAKGI4YTdmNTE5NGM0YjUzZGJkZTg1MTQwMTFlMDMyOWFhNzE0M2Q1NDA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/redhat-developer/rhdh/commit/b1e2f8a1bce196d38f1c9e87793af3304e6c88a0","sha":"b1e2f8a1bce196d38f1c9e87793af3304e6c88a0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redhat-developer/rhdh/commits/b1e2f8a1bce196d38f1c9e87793af3304e6c88a0"}],"sha":"b8a7f5194c4b53dbde8514011e0329aa7143d540","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redhat-developer/rhdh/commits/b8a7f5194c4b53dbde8514011e0329aa7143d540"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1463004?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gustavolira/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gustavolira/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gustavolira/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gustavolira/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gustavolira","id":1463004,"login":"gustavolira","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0NjMwMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gustavolira/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gustavolira/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gustavolira/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gustavolira/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gustavolira/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gustavolira","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redhat-developer/rhdh/commits/b1e2f8a1bce196d38f1c9e87793af3304e6c88a0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-18T20:06:48Z","email":"guga.java@gmail.com","name":"Gustavo Lira e Silva"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-18T20:06:48Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(e2e): surface uncaught page errors when the app bootstrap hangs (#5436)\n\n* fix(e2e): surface uncaught page errors when the app bootstrap hangs\n\nNightly OCP runs intermittently fail with the page stuck on the initial\nMuiCircularProgress spinner for the full 120s timeout. Playwright traces\nshow the real cause is an uncaught bootstrap error (currently a TDZ\nReferenceError in the global-header dynamic plugin chunk), which the\ntoBeHidden timeout hides behind N unrelated test titles.\n\nCollect pageerror events from before page.goto and, when the spinner is\nstill visible after an uncaught error plus a grace period, fail\nimmediately with the actual JS error instead of burning the timeout and\nretries.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(e2e): race the auto-waiting assertion with the page-error watcher; add unit tests\n\nReview follow-ups on the fail-fast mechanism:\n- Keep expect(...).toBeHidden() as the primary wait and race it against a\n  timer-based watcher, so the no-error path keeps its exact previous\n  behavior and failure message.\n- Reset collected errors on domcontentloaded instead of framenavigated:\n  framenavigated also fires for client-side route changes, which would wipe\n  a just-captured bootstrap crash mid-wait.\n- The watcher never waits on the page, so a crashed or closed page cannot\n  mask the real error (it reports <page closed> instead).\n- watchPageErrors returns the live error array (removes a dead ?? [] branch\n  that could silently disconnect the fail-fast).\n- One shared timeout budget across loading indicators; error messages are\n  deduped and capped, and include page.url().\n- Unit tests in e2e-tests/unit/app-shell.test.ts (validated fail-first by\n  mutation: inverting the stuck check turns 3 tests red).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(e2e): reset captured page errors explicitly at navigation, not on events\n\nReview follow-up (hopehadfield): clearing on domcontentloaded wiped\nerrors thrown while the new document was still loading — exactly the\nbootstrap crashes this mechanism exists to expose. Resetting on\nmain-frame navigation events is not viable either: framenavigated also\nfires for client-side route changes, which would wipe a just-captured\ncrash mid-wait.\n\nDrop the event listener entirely and reset explicitly right before the\npage.goto calls in the sign-in helpers — the navigation points we\ncontrol. Unit tests now cover an error emitted before domcontentloaded\n(retained; goes red if the old listener is reintroduced) and across\nclient-side navigations.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"6a51c4969d2cb63e2d6bb31353542b7c475ab4da","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redhat-developer/rhdh/git/trees/6a51c4969d2cb63e2d6bb31353542b7c475ab4da"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redhat-developer/rhdh/git/commits/b1e2f8a1bce196d38f1c9e87793af3304e6c88a0","verification":{"payload":"tree 6a51c4969d2cb63e2d6bb31353542b7c475ab4da\nparent b4eab2988824b146d8944e50e538856f2f6ffa6c\nauthor Gustavo Lira e Silva <guga.java@gmail.com> 1789762008 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789762008 +0000\n\nfix(e2e): surface uncaught page errors when the app bootstrap hangs (#5436)\n\n* fix(e2e): surface uncaught page errors when the app bootstrap hangs\n\nNightly OCP runs intermittently fail with the page stuck on the initial\nMuiCircularProgress spinner for the full 120s timeout. Playwright traces\nshow the real cause is an uncaught bootstrap error (currently a TDZ\nReferenceError in the global-header dynamic plugin chunk), which the\ntoBeHidden timeout hides behind N unrelated test titles.\n\nCollect pageerror events from before page.goto and, when the spinner is\nstill visible after an uncaught error plus a grace period, fail\nimmediately with the actual JS error instead of burning the timeout and\nretries.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(e2e): race the auto-waiting assertion with the page-error watcher; add unit tests\n\nReview follow-ups on the fail-fast mechanism:\n- Keep expect(...).toBeHidden() as the primary wait and race it against a\n  timer-based watcher, so the no-error path keeps its exact previous\n  behavior and failure message.\n- Reset collected errors on domcontentloaded instead of framenavigated:\n  framenavigated also fires for client-side route changes, which would wipe\n  a just-captured bootstrap crash mid-wait.\n- The watcher never waits on the page, so a crashed or closed page cannot\n  mask the real error (it reports <page closed> instead).\n- watchPageErrors returns the live error array (removes a dead ?? [] branch\n  that could silently disconnect the fail-fast).\n- One shared timeout budget across loading indicators; error messages are\n  deduped and capped, and include page.url().\n- Unit tests in e2e-tests/unit/app-shell.test.ts (validated fail-first by\n  mutation: inverting the stuck check turns 3 tests red).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(e2e): reset captured page errors explicitly at navigation, not on events\n\nReview follow-up (hopehadfield): clearing on domcontentloaded wiped\nerrors thrown while the new document was still loading — exactly the\nbootstrap crashes this mechanism exists to expose. Resetting on\nmain-frame navigation events is not viable either: framenavigated also\nfires for client-side route changes, which would wipe a just-captured\ncrash mid-wait.\n\nDrop the event listener entirely and reset explicitly right before the\npage.goto calls in the sign-in helpers — the navigation points we\ncontrol. Unit tests now cover an error emitted before domcontentloaded\n(retained; goes red if the old listener is reintroduced) and across\nclient-side navigations.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqrZnYC