4447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/redhat-developer/rhdh/commit/5b9bfdef9373a085d5f3ae6d8709a8ebe386703d","node_id":"C_kwDOI1ELK9oAKDViOWJmZGVmOTM3M2EwODVkNWYzYWU2ZDg3MDlhOGViZTM4NjcwM2Q","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/redhat-developer/rhdh/commit/487a395b39fb097f763acc95f08f0fd28afbe7c4","sha":"487a395b39fb097f763acc95f08f0fd28afbe7c4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redhat-developer/rhdh/commits/487a395b39fb097f763acc95f08f0fd28afbe7c4"}],"sha":"5b9bfdef9373a085d5f3ae6d8709a8ebe386703d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redhat-developer/rhdh/commits/5b9bfdef9373a085d5f3ae6d8709a8ebe386703d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1463004?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gustavolira/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gustavolira/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gustavolira/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gustavolira/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gustavolira","id":1463004,"login":"gustavolira","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0NjMwMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gustavolira/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gustavolira/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gustavolira/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gustavolira/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gustavolira/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gustavolira","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redhat-developer/rhdh/commits/487a395b39fb097f763acc95f08f0fd28afbe7c4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T18:54:32Z","email":"guga.java@gmail.com","name":"Gustavo Lira e Silva"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T18:54:32Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(docs): repair the dead links across docs and README (#5383)\n\n* fix(docs): repair three broken anchors and one dead link\n\n`markdown-link-check` has failed on every PR since 2026-09-10. Not because of\nanything those PRs changed — it scans the whole repo — but because #5360 bumped\nthe action from v1.1.2 to v1.1.3 the day before, and the newer version checks\nin-file anchors.\n\nWhat it found is real. The three anchors point at\n\n    ### Adding application drawers (`application/internal/drawer-*`)\n\nwhose slug keeps the hyphen before the asterisk and so ends in one. The links\nomit it, which means they have been going nowhere on GitHub since the guides\nlanded in July (#5009). Verified with github-slugger rather than reasoned about.\nIt is the only heading in docs/ that falls into this trap.\n\nbackstage.io/docs/reference/filter-predicates is a genuine 404 with no successor\nI could find, so the link goes and the sentence keeps its wording rather than\npointing somewhere invented.\n\ndocs.redhat.com is the one false positive, and it is intermittent rather than a\nflat block: the two URLs that failed in CI answer 200 from a workstation, and\nanswered 302/403 an hour earlier. The site rate-limits automated callers, and\nthe existing retry settings only cover 429, not 403. Ignoring the domain is the\npragmatic fix, at the cost of no longer checking the six docs.redhat.com links\nin the repo — the other four are passing today and would lose coverage.\n\nVerified by running markdown-link-check with the repo''s own config over each\naffected file: all exit 0.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(docs): repair the dead links across docs and README\n\n`markdown-link-check` has failed on every PR since 2026-09-10, against content\nnone of those PRs touched — it scans the whole repo. #5360 bumped the action\nfrom v1.1.2 to v1.1.3 the day before and the newer version checks in-file\nanchors, which is what surfaced the first batch.\n\nAnchors. Three links point at\n\n    ### Adding application drawers (`application/internal/drawer-*`)\n\nwhose slug keeps the hyphen before the asterisk and so ends in one. They have\nbeen going nowhere on GitHub since the guides landed in July (#5009). Verified\nwith github-slugger; it is the only heading in docs/ with this shape.\n\nPages that moved upstream:\n- backstage.io/docs/reference/filter-predicates -> the generated API reference\n  (thanks Hope for finding it)\n- backstage.io/docs/reference/core-plugin-api.apptheme -> the module page, the\n  hand-written reference page is gone\n- docs.ci.openshift.org/docs/architecture/prow -> /docs/architecture\n- community-plugins redhat-argocd -> argocd, renamed in their #6820\n- community-plugins github-actions, github-issues and\n  github-pull-requests-board -> all under one github workspace after their #7507\n- gajus/global-agent test files -> the repo root; neither path exists on master\n  or main any more\n\nThings that no longer exist here:\n- values_showcase-auth-providers.yaml was deleted in #4458, and the bullet above\n  it already says that job deploys with the Operator rather than Helm, so the\n  whole bullet goes\n- github-discovery.spec.ts is gone; the auth-providers suites are what use\n  fixtures today\n\nRate-limited hosts, not dead links: docs.redhat.com, developers.redhat.com and\ndevservices.dpp.openshift.com answer 200 or resolve from a workstation and 403\nor 0 from CI. The existing retry settings only cover 429. They join the two Red\nHat hosts already in ignorePatterns, at the cost of no longer checking the\nhandful of links behind them.\n\nVerified by running markdown-link-check with the repo''s own config over docs/\nand the root markdown, the two sets the workflow checks: both clean.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"0191a25c9e626520a39fd975306713fb41121acd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redhat-developer/rhdh/git/trees/0191a25c9e626520a39fd975306713fb41121acd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redhat-developer/rhdh/git/commits/487a395b39fb097f763acc95f08f0fd28afbe7c4","verification":{"payload":"tree 0191a25c9e626520a39fd975306713fb41121acd\nparent 1e73ec12eaede991386fb95cb4a0e5ba7015867d\nauthor Gustavo Lira e Silva <guga.java@gmail.com> 1789412072 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789412072 -0400\n\nfix(docs): repair the dead links across docs and README (#5383)\n\n* fix(docs): repair three broken anchors and one dead link\n\n`markdown-link-check` has failed on every PR since 2026-09-10. Not because of\nanything those PRs changed — it scans the whole repo — but because #5360 bumped\nthe action from v1.1.2 to v1.1.3 the day before, and the newer version checks\nin-file anchors.\n\nWhat it found is real. The three anchors point at\n\n    ### Adding application drawers (`application/internal/drawer-*`)\n\nwhose slug keeps the hyphen before the asterisk and so ends in one. The links\nomit it, which means they have been going nowhere on GitHub since the guides\nlanded in July (#5009). Verified with github-slugger rather than reasoned about.\nIt is the only heading in docs/ that falls into this trap.\n\nbackstage.io/docs/reference/filter-predicates is a genuine 404 with no successor\nI could find, so the link goes and the sentence keeps its wording rather than\npointing somewhere invented.\n\ndocs.redhat.com is the one false positive, and it is intermittent rather than a\nflat block: the two URLs that failed in CI answer 200 from a workstation, and\nanswered 302/403 an hour earlier. The site rate-limits automated callers, and\nthe existing retry settings only cover 429, not 403. Ignoring the domain is the\npragmatic fix, at the cost of no longer checking the six docs.redhat.com links\nin the repo — the other four are passing today and would lose coverage.\n\nVerified by running markdown-link-check with the repo''s own config over each\naffected file: all exit 0.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(docs): repair the dead links across docs and README\n\n`markdown-link-check` has failed on every PR since 2026-09-10, against content\nnone of those PRs touched — it scans the whole repo. #5360 bumped the action\nfrom v1.1.2 to v1.1.3 the day before and the newer version checks in-file\nanchors, which is what surfaced the first batch.\n\nAnchors. Three links point at\n\n    ### Adding application drawers (`application/internal/drawer-*`)\n\nwhose slug keeps the hyphen before the asterisk and so ends in one. They have\nbeen going nowhere on GitHub since the guides landed in July (#5009). Verified\nwith github-slugger; it is the only heading in docs/ with this shape.\n\nPages that moved upstream:\n- backstage.io/docs/reference/filter-predicates -> the generated API reference\n  (thanks Hope for finding it)\n- backstage.io/docs/reference/core-plugin-api.apptheme -> the module page, the\n  hand-written reference page is gone\n- docs.ci.openshift.org/docs/architecture/prow -> /docs/architecture\n- community-plugins redhat-argocd -> argocd, renamed in their #6820\n- community-plugins github-actions, github-issues and\n  github-pull-requests-board -> all under one github workspace after their #7507\n- gajus/global-agent test files -> the repo root; neither path exists on master\n  or main any more\n\nThings that no longer exist here:\n- values_showcase-auth-providers.yaml was deleted in #4458, and the bullet above\n  it already says that job deploys with the Operator rather than Helm, so the\n  whole bullet goes\n- github-discovery.spec.ts is gone; the auth-providers suites are what use\n  fixtures today\n\nRate-limited hosts, not dead links: docs.redhat.com, developers.redhat.com and\ndevservices.dpp.openshift.com answer 200 or resolve from a workstation and 403\nor 0 from CI. The existing retry settings only cover 429. They join the two Red\nHat hosts already in ignorePatterns, at the cost of no longer checking the\nhandful of links behind them.\n\nVerified by running markdown-link-check with the repo''s own config over docs/\nand the root markdown, the two sets the workflow checks: both clean.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqqELoCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAqUEQAC2nCv1gXl/AHGmsZ8ndByR0\nta7PhRhknwCpWgFmTaZrsFT8YgL1npeB6sVuhmOmVflRXzAzAW3mtOFvEwl5Qpoo\nvzyE8TRnX254jiGthSGEeFhl5IA81bzDRoBcW7pMs1eBYFMZLnCwSr+ZfjOKCM0O\nfrsukrEw5xhh4Pz7WP0YFZSTSSlB1AWY+WNrpPzGLngmxPfg+EcW0JLeo0HSgNL8\nx0DB6LWTGK+j/x3fAuI3X1K9BrT8jAmGSU6f8Glqpm6QrAc1cKKCeJuEUC44OZYx\nT9YcQFHnAPy61JKk0jFaqBpAVWJs620E9lYynGPUSlQxFboDwGCpH3ya3b4VhKez\nzgewjIbhu6C9kcMcO8C1EbQtbcHgixtNn1dfkbiAOLPrHadU/jLIjc2sxqnq4tg1\nO/WsWUiJCGto4KQ3HQUmITS2r9IKKDiESnSnBQrHz12mJHUYKK922SpCwW302ctY\nRL3mm3M1Ac5oREw8TIH/N2K2kn7rc832dLslvchFfjTmlHoIUvr/XPFZ13TlT6L5\nZX8dTyAYTVj+Wczypb6be2LvDR4p1CijXE3IQ7WbQn2DzVtWCQ63pMmri2hcdbG1\nnLffFScmRxG/w+Tf7me18OCffIoJzrBIs7twp485sg8jXzv0vB40dIBOZ0vvEtS1\n1qQf2mPe7CQmGQCe4AkC\n=TgIS\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-14T18:54:33Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/oth