62540a32d6d7a9f7f989009ae99009","node_id":"C_kwDOI32GJNoAKDk5YWNlZWE4MDc2MjU0MGEzMmQ2ZDdhOWY3Zjk4OTAwOWFlOTkwMDk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/AhmedTakeshy/My-protfolio/commit/990f45f2c1dc0a82e62ee348df56d8ae6a17fce1","sha":"990f45f2c1dc0a82e62ee348df56d8ae6a17fce1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AhmedTakeshy/My-protfolio/commits/990f45f2c1dc0a82e62ee348df56d8ae6a17fce1"}],"sha":"99aceea80762540a32d6d7a9f7f989009ae99009","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AhmedTakeshy/My-protfolio/commits/99aceea80762540a32d6d7a9f7f989009ae99009"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/37537011?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/AhmedTakeshy","id":37537011,"login":"AhmedTakeshy","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM3NTM3MDEx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AhmedTakeshy/My-protfolio/commits/990f45f2c1dc0a82e62ee348df56d8ae6a17fce1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-12T06:47:01Z","email":"Ahmedtakeshy7@gmail.com","name":"AhmedTakeshy"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-12T06:47:01Z","email":"Ahmedtakeshy7@gmail.com","name":"AhmedTakeshy"},"message":"fix(pipeline): prevent horizontal overflow on narrow phones\n\nFive fixed-width nodes (w-16 = 64px each) plus connector margins summed\nto ~352px minimum, but a 375px viewport only has ~345px of content\nwidth after the site''s 15px container padding on each side -- an\noverflow that existed even in the best case (connectors compressed to\nzero width). Shrink the node column, icon box, and connector margins\nat the default breakpoint, sizing back up at sm/lg, so the row fits\ncomfortably down to the smallest common phone widths.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NxF5c9Swv9TgFt5gDt8xvJ","tree":{"sha":"76f742e5b22716d8004adbcccf1852896d8bd960","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AhmedTakeshy/My-protfolio/git/trees/76f742e5b22716d8004adbcccf1852896d8bd960"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AhmedTakeshy/My-protfolio/git/commits/990f45f2c1dc0a82e62ee348df56d8ae6a17fce1","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/37537011?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/AhmedTakeshy","id":37537011,"login":"AhmedTakeshy","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM3NTM3MDEx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/AhmedTakeshy/My-protfolio/commit/990f45f2c1dc0a82e62ee348df56d8ae6a17fce1","node_id":"C_kwDOI32GJNoAKDk5MGY0NWYyYzFkYzBhODJlNjJlZTM0OGRmNTZkOGFlNmExN2ZjZTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/AhmedTakeshy/My-protfolio/commit/7944f58aef238120d36c77d464fd5608c8e9b9e0","sha":"7944f58aef238120d36c77d464fd5608c8e9b9e0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AhmedTakeshy/My-protfolio/commits/7944f58aef238120d36c77d464fd5608c8e9b9e0"}],"sha":"990f45f2c1dc0a82e62ee348df56d8ae6a17fce1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AhmedTakeshy/My-protfolio/commits/990f45f2c1dc0a82e62ee348df56d8ae6a17fce1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/37537011?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/AhmedTakeshy","id":37537011,"login":"AhmedTakeshy","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM3NTM3MDEx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AhmedTakeshy/My-protfolio/commits/7944f58aef238120d36c77d464fd5608c8e9b9e0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-12T06:24:53Z","email":"Ahmedtakeshy7@gmail.com","name":"AhmedTakeshy"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-12T06:24:53Z","email":"Ahmedtakeshy7@gmail.com","name":"AhmedTakeshy"},"message":"feat(depth): sitewide 3D scroll identity -- perspective, parallax grid, tilt reveals, hero diagram tilt\n\nFour pieces, all real CSS 3D transforms / scroll-linked Framer Motion,\nno canvas or video frame-scrubbing (that technique is built for\nvideo-like content; ours is vector, so useTransform against\nuseScroll''s progress value gives the same scroll-locked feel with a\nfraction of the weight):\n\n1. Shared perspective context set locally on each grid/flex container\n   that hosts reveal animations (CaseStudies, Capabilities, LiveMetrics,\n   About, Contact, Hero''s diagram wrapper) -- same 1200px value\n   everywhere so it reads as one consistent 3D space rather than\n   scattered effects.\n\n2. A second, finer blueprint-grid layer (globals.css: .blueprint-grid-fine)\n   positioned absolute (scrolls with the document) layered over the\n   existing fixed coarse grid (never moves). The relative motion between\n   a 0x-speed layer and a 1x-speed layer is real parallax depth, with\n   zero scroll-linked JS.\n\n3. ScrollReveal upgraded from a flat opacity/translateY fade to a\n   settle-into-place tilt: starts at rotateX(10deg) scale(0.96), settles\n   to flat/full-size as it enters view. Applied everywhere it already\n   ran (CaseStudies, Capabilities) and newly wired into About, Contact,\n   and LiveMetrics, which previously had no scroll animation at all.\n\n4. The hero ArchitectureDiagram -- the site''s signature element -- now\n   tilts in real 3D (rotateY, scale, opacity) driven by scroll progress\n   through the hero section specifically (useScroll scoped to a local\n   ref, not the whole page), fading and rotating away as the visitor\n   scrolls into Live Metrics. Respects prefers-reduced-motion the same\n   way Pipeline.tsx does (a static motion value swapped in for the real\n   scroll progress).\n\nVerified in a real browser across the full page (Hero through Footer)\nin both dev and a production build/start, including that the Contact\nform''s inputs stayed interactive after restructuring its layout to\ncarry ScrollReveal correctly.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NxF5c9Swv9TgFt5gDt8xvJ","tree":{"sha":"4bcbb6b291f25d0a423ce9bac53ada0d23af0fce","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AhmedTakeshy/My-protfolio/git/trees/4bcbb6b291f25d0a423ce9bac53ada0d23af0fce"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AhmedTakeshy/My-protfolio/git/commits/7944f58aef238120d36c77d464fd5608c8e9b9e0","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/37537011?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/AhmedTakeshy","id":37537011,"login":"AhmedTakeshy","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM3NTM3MDEx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/AhmedTakeshy/My-protfolio/commit/7944f58aef238120d36c77d464fd5608c8e9b9e0","node_id":"C_kwDOI32GJNoAKDc5NDRmNThhZWYyMzgxMjBkMzZjNzdkNDY0ZmQ1NjA4YzhlOWI5ZTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/AhmedTakeshy/My-protfolio/commit/8a9469d64f99637e08679f588eca60dd8c6305ec","sha":"8a9469d64f99637e08679f588eca60dd8c6305ec","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AhmedTakeshy/My-protfolio/commits/8a9469d64f99637e08679f588eca60dd8c6305ec"}],"sha":"7944f58aef238120d36c77d464fd5608c8e9b9e0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AhmedTakeshy/My-protfolio/commits/7944f58aef238120d36c77d464fd5608c8e9b9e0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/37537011?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/AhmedTakeshy","id":37537011,"login":"AhmedTakeshy","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM3NTM3MDEx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AhmedTakeshy/My-protfolio/commits/8a9469d64f99637e08679f588eca60dd8c6305ec/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-12T05:47:46Z","email":"Ahmedtakeshy7@gmail.com","name":"AhmedTakeshy"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-12T05:47:46Z","email":"Ahmedtakeshy7@gmail.com","name":"AhmedTakeshy"},"message":"feat(pipeline): add scroll-driven CI/CD pipeline strip between Live and Work\n\nAdd a \"the pipeline behind the work\" section: five stage nodes (COMMIT\n→ BUILD → TEST → DEPLOY → LIVE) that light up in sequence as the\nvisitor scrolls, connected by a fill line, with small accent-tinted\nsquares scattered across the background that pop in as the pipeline\nruns -- the sitewide blueprint grid \"waking up.\" Stage captions reuse\nElonky''s real, already-verified numbers (16min->1.5min build, 85% E2E\ncoverage, 60% fewer bugs) rather than invented figures, so the\nanimation is the same true pipeline the Work section explains in full.\n\nBuilt with Framer Motion''s useScroll/useTransform against vector\nelements only (no canvas/image sequence), consistent with the site''s\nown live-performance claims.\n\nFix a real bug found while building this: useTransform on the first\npipeline node computed a degenerate [0, 0] input range (from an\nunnecessary Math.max(threshold - 0.1, 0) clamp), which broke Framer\nMotion''s shared animation scheduler and silently stalled the Hero''s\nfade-in across the whole page. Removing the clamp (negative bounds are\nvalid interpolation inputs) fixes it for all nodes.\n\nAlso fix Nav.tsx: its hardcoded section indices (00-04) had drifted\nout of sync with the actual section eyebrows after the Live Metrics\nsection was added last commit. Added a Live entry and renumbered to\nmatch (00 Home, 01 Live, 02 Work, 03 Capabilities, 04 About, 05 Contact).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NxF5c9Swv9TgFt5gDt8xvJ","tree":{"sha":"9aa5f673c662e54d2003b8784c4d558936e722b5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AhmedTakeshy/My-protfolio/git/trees/9aa5f673c662e54d2003b8784c4d558936e722b5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AhmedTakeshy/My-protfolio/git/commits/8a9469d64f99637e08679f588eca60dd8c6305ec","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/37537011?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/AhmedTakeshy","id":37537011,"login":"AhmedTakeshy","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM3NTM3MDEx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/AhmedTakeshy/My-protfolio/commit/8a9469d64f99637e08679f588eca60dd8c6305ec","node_id":"C_kwDOI32GJNoAKDhhOTQ2OWQ2NGY5OTYzN2UwODY3OWY1ODhlY2E2MGRkOGM2MzA1ZWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/AhmedTakeshy/My-protfolio/commit/c2e545d2cd4809067246d337d5ac7af684b2e7c0","sha":"c2e545d2cd4809067246d337d5ac7af684b2e7c0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AhmedTakeshy/My-protfolio/commits/c2e545d2cd4809067246d337d5ac7af684b2e7c0"}],"sha":"8a9469d64f99637e08679f588eca60dd8c6305ec","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AhmedTakeshy/My-protfolio/commits/8a9469d64f99637e08679f588eca60dd8c6305ec"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/37537011?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/AhmedTakeshy","id":37537011,"login":"AhmedTakeshy","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM3NTM3MDEx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AhmedTakeshy/My-protfolio/commits/c2e545d2cd4809067246d337d5ac7af684b2e7c0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-12T05:06:07Z","email":"Ahmedtakeshy7@gmail.com","name":"AhmedTakeshy"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-12T05:06:07Z","email":"Ahmedtakeshy7@gmail.com","name":"AhmedTakeshy"},"message":"feat(live-metrics): add real, live Core Web Vitals section\n\nAdd a \"01 — Live\" section right after the hero that measures this\npage''s own LCP, INP, CLS, and TTFB in the visitor''s own browser via\nthe official web-vitals library, with reportAllChanges so the numbers\nvisibly update in front of the visitor instead of only finalizing on\ntab-hide.\n\nThis replaces an asserted claim with a verifiable one: instead of\ntelling a hiring manager \"I care about performance,\" the page proves\nit live. INP honestly shows \"waiting for a click or keypress\" until\nthe visitor actually interacts, rather than faking a number.\n\nRenumber the eyebrow labels on the sections that follow (Work,\nCapabilities, About, Contact) to keep the sequence consistent.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NxF5c9Swv9TgFt5gDt8xvJ","tree":{"sha":"fb9ad3d227c42c28293931e710ef1d3dd0261c5c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AhmedTakeshy/My-protfolio/git/trees/fb9ad3d227c42c28293931e710ef1d3dd0261c5c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AhmedTakeshy/My-protfolio/git/commits/c2e545d2cd4809067246d337d5ac7af684b2e7c0","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/37537011?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/events{/privacy}","followers