pi.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AhmedTakeshy/My-protfolio/commits/bdeed4492a9b269a7f0654816aab08088608d378/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T12:11:40Z","email":"Ahmedtakeshy7@gmail.com","name":"AhmedTakeshy"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T12:11:40Z","email":"Ahmedtakeshy7@gmail.com","name":"AhmedTakeshy"},"message":"chore(assets): prune unused images, rebrand favicon/PWA icons\n\n- Delete 18 unreferenced images left over from the old portfolio\n  (old project screenshots, decorative meter/header svgs, site-bg)\n- Regenerate all favicon/PWA icon PNGs (16/32/apple-touch/192/512/\n  maskable) with a new brand mark matching the systems & architecture\n  identity: a chip silhouette with a pin-1 notch, accent orange on\n  the dark navy background, rendered from a single vector source via\n  sharp (already a project dependency)\n- Fix manifest.ts: remove a dead /favicon.ico entry pointing at a\n  file that never existed, and update background_color/theme_color\n  from the old white (#fff) to the dark brand background (#0B0E13)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NxF5c9Swv9TgFt5gDt8xvJ","tree":{"sha":"ed3691f9764d3cd4b8f483f30cd46a43d2a9f961","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AhmedTakeshy/My-protfolio/git/trees/ed3691f9764d3cd4b8f483f30cd46a43d2a9f961"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AhmedTakeshy/My-protfolio/git/commits/bdeed4492a9b269a7f0654816aab08088608d378","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/37537011?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/AhmedTakeshy","id":37537011,"login":"AhmedTakeshy","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM3NTM3MDEx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/AhmedTakeshy/My-protfolio/commit/bdeed4492a9b269a7f0654816aab08088608d378","node_id":"C_kwDOI32GJNoAKGJkZWVkNDQ5MmE5YjI2OWE3ZjA2NTQ4MTZhYWIwODA4ODYwOGQzNzg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/AhmedTakeshy/My-protfolio/commit/4937a4e0bbe71464ec5b581e48dd8094b0f8be92","sha":"4937a4e0bbe71464ec5b581e48dd8094b0f8be92","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AhmedTakeshy/My-protfolio/commits/4937a4e0bbe71464ec5b581e48dd8094b0f8be92"}],"sha":"bdeed4492a9b269a7f0654816aab08088608d378","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AhmedTakeshy/My-protfolio/commits/bdeed4492a9b269a7f0654816aab08088608d378"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/37537011?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/AhmedTakeshy","id":37537011,"login":"AhmedTakeshy","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM3NTM3MDEx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AhmedTakeshy/My-protfolio/commits/4937a4e0bbe71464ec5b581e48dd8094b0f8be92/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T12:01:37Z","email":"Ahmedtakeshy7@gmail.com","name":"AhmedTakeshy"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T12:01:37Z","email":"Ahmedtakeshy7@gmail.com","name":"AhmedTakeshy"},"message":"Add scroll effects and hero diagram polish, informed by real references\n\nDirection: user shared 5 real reference images (architectural\nblueprint/BIM-scan aesthetics). Two were genuinely useful signal\n(status-annotated wireframe diagrams, icon+label+value spec-sheet\nlayouts); the photographic/glitch-text ones were skipped as not\nfitting a software engineer''s portfolio.\n\nHero diagram (ArchitectureDiagram.tsx):\n- Soft SVG glow filter on connecting lines/first node -- subtle,\n  blended back with the source, not a blown-out neon effect\n- Added 3 status readouts styled like a system-scan result (status\n  dot + label + value), directly inspired by the reference boards --\n  but every value is real and already-verified (CI/CD 16m->1.5m, 85%\n  E2E coverage, -60% prod bugs), not decoration\n\nNew scroll effects, designed so motion only ever enhances and can\nnever gate content''s visibility (the lesson from the earlier\nwhileInView bug):\n- ScrollReveal: renders fully visible by default (no-JS = fully\n  visible); only once JS confirms it''s running does it apply a subtle\n  pre-reveal state (opacity 40%, not 0, plus a small offset); a hard\n  1.5s timeout forces full visibility regardless of whether the\n  IntersectionObserver ever fires. Applied to case-study cards and\n  capability groups with a light stagger.\n- ScrollProgress: thin fixed bar tied to scroll position (Framer\n  Motion useScroll) -- purely additive, nothing depends on it.\n- Cursor-tracked spotlight hover on case-study cards (CSS custom\n  properties updated on mousemove, no re-render per frame).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NxF5c9Swv9TgFt5gDt8xvJ","tree":{"sha":"a32927c40d9ac4b0f57ae817032ab66f8db11a04","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AhmedTakeshy/My-protfolio/git/trees/a32927c40d9ac4b0f57ae817032ab66f8db11a04"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AhmedTakeshy/My-protfolio/git/commits/4937a4e0bbe71464ec5b581e48dd8094b0f8be92","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/37537011?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/AhmedTakeshy","id":37537011,"login":"AhmedTakeshy","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM3NTM3MDEx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/AhmedTakeshy/My-protfolio/commit/4937a4e0bbe71464ec5b581e48dd8094b0f8be92","node_id":"C_kwDOI32GJNoAKDQ5MzdhNGUwYmJlNzE0NjRlYzViNTgxZTQ4ZGQ4MDk0YjBmOGJlOTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/AhmedTakeshy/My-protfolio/commit/a72dfc11cb15ba8d6c97be558dcf312a0b3c4951","sha":"a72dfc11cb15ba8d6c97be558dcf312a0b3c4951","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AhmedTakeshy/My-protfolio/commits/a72dfc11cb15ba8d6c97be558dcf312a0b3c4951"}],"sha":"4937a4e0bbe71464ec5b581e48dd8094b0f8be92","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AhmedTakeshy/My-protfolio/commits/4937a4e0bbe71464ec5b581e48dd8094b0f8be92"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/37537011?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/AhmedTakeshy","id":37537011,"login":"AhmedTakeshy","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM3NTM3MDEx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AhmedTakeshy/My-protfolio/commits/a72dfc11cb15ba8d6c97be558dcf312a0b3c4951/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T11:53:16Z","email":"Ahmedtakeshy7@gmail.com","name":"AhmedTakeshy"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T11:53:16Z","email":"Ahmedtakeshy7@gmail.com","name":"AhmedTakeshy"},"message":"Upgrade Next.js 15 canary -> 16.3.4, React/React-DOM -> 19.3.0\n\nVercel flagged the deployed Next.js canary as a known-vulnerable\nversion and blocked/warned on deploy. Upgraded the important pieces\nas scoped: Next.js, React, React-DOM, and their required companions\n(@next/bundle-analyzer, @next/third-parties, eslint-config-next) --\nTailwind stays on v3 for now, deferred separately (v4 is a config-model\nmigration, not a drop-in bump, and isn''t implicated in this vulnerability).\nAlso bumped `sharp` (0.33.5 -> 0.35.4) to clear unrelated known CVEs in\nits bundled libvips/libheif -- build-time only, not application code.//\n`npm audit` now reports 0 vulnerabilities.\n\nReal breaking changes found and fixed via actual build/runtime testing,\nnot just \"it compiled\":\n\n- `experimental.ppr` was merged into top-level `cacheComponents` --\n  updated next.config.ts.\n- cacheComponents'' stricter prerendering rejected `new Date()` in\n  Footer''s static render (a real catch: that value can change between\n  requests). Made Footer a client component so it resolves in the\n  browser instead.\n- The cookies()-reading Suspense boundary I''d added for the cookie\n  consent banner hit a real Next 16 PPR issue in production only (not\n  reproducible in dev): \"the server could not finish this Suspense\n  boundary... switched to client rendering\" (React error #419). Fixed\n  by making the whole banner client-side via useSyncExternalStore\n  (the correct primitive for a browser-only source like document.cookie)\n  instead of fighting PPR for a feature with zero SSR/SEO value. Net\n  result is better than before: the homepage is now fully static (was\n  partially dynamic even before this session''s PPR experiment).\n- eslint-config-next 16 ships native flat config; the old FlatCompat\n  bridge in eslint.config.mjs crashed against it (circular structure\n  in a validation-error path) -- switched to importing the flat\n  configs directly.\n- `react-hooks/set-state-in-effect` (a newer rule) caught a genuinely\n  redundant client-side cookie re-read in cookies.tsx; removed it\n  rather than suppressing the lint rule.\n- Committed the new AGENTS.md/CLAUDE.md files Next 16 auto-generates\n  (guardrails for AI agents against outdated training data) -- the\n  tool''s own header says to commit them.\n- tsconfig.json''s mandatory `jsx: react-jsx` change and new\n  `.next/dev/types` include, both applied automatically by the\n  Next 16 build.\n\nVerified via real build + production server + Playwright, not just a\ngreen build: hero, cookie-consent interaction (accept -> banner\ndisappears, cookie persists), and the case-study modal all confirmed\nworking after the upgrade.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NxF5c9Swv9TgFt5gDt8xvJ","tree":{"sha":"f0ac5e73dd203c0ab2142c30ad78825483148920","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AhmedTakeshy/My-protfolio/git/trees/f0ac5e73dd203c0ab2142c30ad78825483148920"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AhmedTakeshy/My-protfolio/git/commits/a72dfc11cb15ba8d6c97be558dcf312a0b3c4951","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/37537011?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/AhmedTakeshy","id":37537011,"login":"AhmedTakeshy","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM3NTM3MDEx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/AhmedTakeshy/My-protfolio/commit/a72dfc11cb15ba8d6c97be558dcf312a0b3c4951","node_id":"C_kwDOI32GJNoAKGE3MmRmYzExY2IxNWJhOGQ2Yzk3YmU1NThkY2YzMTJhMGIzYzQ5NTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/AhmedTakeshy/My-protfolio/commit/84740455a8a5c3a729ee99cb07c7e3c42940053f","sha":"84740455a8a5c3a729ee99cb07c7e3c42940053f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AhmedTakeshy/My-protfolio/commits/84740455a8a5c3a729ee99cb07c7e3c42940053f"}],"sha":"a72dfc11cb15ba8d6c97be558dcf312a0b3c4951","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AhmedTakeshy/My-protfolio/commits/a72dfc11cb15ba8d6c97be558dcf312a0b3c4951"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/37537011?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/AhmedTakeshy","id":37537011,"login":"AhmedTakeshy","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM3NTM3MDEx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AhmedTakeshy/My-protfolio/commits/84740455a8a5c3a729ee99cb07c7e3c42940053f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T11:31:06Z","email":"Ahmedtakeshy7@gmail.com","name":"AhmedTakeshy"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T11:31:06Z","email":"Ahmedtakeshy7@gmail.com","name":"AhmedTakeshy"},"message":"Add engines.node for Vercel Node.js version compliance\n\nVercel''s build was failing: \"Found invalid or discontinued Node.js\nVersion: 18.x. Please set Node.js Version to 24.x in your Project\nSettings.\" This is a Vercel platform runtime setting, not a package\nversion issue -- no dependency upgrade would have fixed this.\n\nAdded engines.node as a fallback signal, but the authoritative fix\nis the Project Settings -> General -> Node.js Version dashboard field\nitself (no MCP/API surface exposes it for a direct fix here).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NxF5c9Swv9TgFt5gDt8xvJ","tree":{"sha":"0fbe55f8e6324cb00189d23a92f63515f1714637","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AhmedTakeshy/My-protfolio/git/trees/0fbe55f8e6324cb00189d23a92f63515f1714637"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AhmedTakeshy/My-protfolio/git/commits/84740455a8a5c3a729ee99cb07c7e3c42940053f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/37537011?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/AhmedTakeshy","id":37537011,"login":"AhmedTakeshy","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM3NTM3MDEx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/AhmedTakeshy/My-protfolio/commit/84740455a8a5c3a729ee99cb07c7e3c42940053f","node_id":"C_kwDOI32GJNoAKDg0NzQwNDU1YThhNWMzYTcyOWVlOTljYjA3YzdlM2M0Mjk0MDA1M2Y","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/AhmedTakeshy/My-protfolio/commit/f51e2b36b2bc198e335b4ce2fd214d2d45032fad","sha":"f51e2b36b2bc198e335b4ce2fd214d2d45032fad","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AhmedTakeshy/My-protfolio/commits/f51e2b36b2bc198e335b4ce2fd214d2d45032fad"}],"sha":"84740455a8a5c3a729ee99cb07c7e3c42940053f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AhmedTakeshy/My-protfolio/commits/84740455a8a5c3a729ee99cb07c7e3c42940053f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/37537011?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/AhmedTakeshy","id":37537011,"login":"AhmedTakeshy","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM3NTM3MDEx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedTakeshy","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AhmedTakeshy/My-protfolio/commits/f51e2b36b2bc198e335b4ce2fd214d2d45032fad/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T11:27:03Z","email":"Ahmedtakeshy7@gmail.com","name":"AhmedTakeshy"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T11:27:03Z","email":"Ahmedtakeshy7@gmail.com","name":"AhmedTakeshy"},"message":"Fix: grid invisible + reduce entrance-animation overlap risk\n\nTwo real bugs found from live testing on localhost:\n\n1. The site-wide blueprint grid was completely invisible. Root cause:\n   the page wrapper div had both `relative` and `bg-bg`. A\n   position:relative element (even without z-index) paints its own\n   background at a later stacking step than a negative-z-index child,\n   so the wrapper''s solid bg-bg was painting over the fixed grid layer\n   underneath it. Fix: drop bg-bg from the wrapper (body already sets\n   it) so nothing paints over the grid.\n\n2. Reduced the hero''s fadeIn distance (80px -> 16px) and duration\n   (1.2s -> 0.5s). Stacked text elements sliding up 80px with\n   staggered per-element delays can visually cross over each other\n   before settling into their normal-flow position -- a plausible\n   cause of the overlapping-text report. Smaller distance + shorter\n   duration removes the risk rather than just reducing its odds.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NxF5c9Swv9TgFt5gDt8xvJ","tree":{"sha":"fedbc5515b8131866620ffebaa22b009ba856013","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AhmedTakeshy/My-protfolio/git/trees/fedbc5515b8131866620ffebaa22b009ba856013"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AhmedTakeshy/My-protfolio/git/commits/f51e2b36b2bc198e335b4ce2fd214d2d45032fad","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/37537011?v=4","events_url"